WEBVTT

1
00:00:02,211 --> 00:00:04,543
[♪ Marvel Studios fanfare
playing]

2
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:39,612
[wind howling]

3
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:47,089
[sighs]

4
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:51,131
[Yelena] <i>There is something
Wrong with me.</i>

5
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,432
<i>An emptiness.</i>

6
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:04,145
<i>I thought it started
when my sister died,</i>

7
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:07,223
<i>but now it feels
like something bigger.</i>

8
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:13,108
<i>Just a... void.</i>

9
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:24,911
<i>Or maybe I'm just bored.</i>

10
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:29,662
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

11
00:01:41,685 --> 00:01:42,675
Boo.

12
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:45,845
[both grunting]

13
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:50,141
[Yelena groans]

14
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,270
<i>They send me a job,</i>

15
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,272
<i>I clock in, clock out,
you know?</i>

16
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:56,947
[guards shouting]

17
00:01:58,660 --> 00:01:59,946
[gun fires]

18
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:02,699
<i>I'm in the cleanup business.</i>

19
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:07,537
<i>This week, Malaysia.
Next week, who knows?</i>

20
00:02:09,338 --> 00:02:12,205
<i>I thought throwing myself
Info work was the answer.</i>

21
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:17,710
<i>But I'm not focused,
and I'm not happy,</i>

22
00:02:17,805 --> 00:02:19,341
<i>and I don't have purpose.</i>

23
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:24,096
<i>And without purpose, I'm just
drifting like a river...</i>

24
00:02:24,186 --> 00:02:25,347
[gun fires]

25
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,851
...or like an old leaf.

26
00:02:31,735 --> 00:02:33,567
Or like an old leaf
in a river.

27
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:35,144
Which do you think is bet--
'Ey!

28
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,238
You weren't listening to me.

29
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:40,487
It's like your mind
is somewhere else.

30
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:41,567
[whimpers]

31
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:44,324
Well, whatever.
You're useless to me unless

32
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:47,406
you can get me past that
facial recognition thingy.

33
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:50,208
[sighs]

34
00:02:50,838 --> 00:02:51,953
[guard exclaims]

35
00:02:56,468 --> 00:02:57,458
[gasps]

36
00:02:58,595 --> 00:02:59,847
Hello.

37
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:01,887
Can you help me get in there?

38
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,090
No?

39
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:05,675
Mmm.

40
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:07,851
You've got your own problems,
I guess.

41
00:03:09,064 --> 00:03:11,226
Well, it didn't say how
to destroy the evidence

42
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:12,693
in the assignment.

43
00:03:12,776 --> 00:03:13,857
It's gonna get messy.

44
00:03:13,944 --> 00:03:15,434
[lab tech] Stop right there!

45
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:23,484
Hi.

46
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,124
Now, that's a face
that can open a scanner.

47
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:28,743
Did Valentina send you?

48
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:31,075
This research is property
of OXE Group.

49
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:32,159
You're gonna tell me

50
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:33,585
- I don't understand.
- You don't understand.

51
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,458
- We've made a breakthrough.
- You've made a breakthrough.

52
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:37,381
- It's gonna change the world.
- No, no, no.

53
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,844
- It could end the world.
- Blah, blah, blah.

54
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:41,419
Valentina doesn't
understand what happened here.

55
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:43,174
Shh, shh, shh.

56
00:03:43,265 --> 00:03:46,053
Look, blame the US government
for their pesky investigation.

57
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:48,805
Now we have to get rid
of all this stuff.

58
00:03:48,896 --> 00:03:50,182
Do you think
I like taking orders?

59
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:53,606
Going from job to job doing
the same thing all the time?

60
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:56,059
Don't do it.
I wouldn't do that.

61
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:00,859
Always a struggle for a gun.

62
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:03,198
[lab tech] Oh, God.

63
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:04,992
[gunshots]

64
00:04:06,538 --> 00:04:08,324
You shoot, I dodge.

65
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:09,701
[lab tech] Oh, my God.

66
00:04:11,126 --> 00:04:13,242
Tell Valentina
she's making a mistake.

67
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,120
- [grunts]
- [gunshots]

68
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:17,204
[lab tech exclaims]

69
00:04:17,299 --> 00:04:18,755
You guys can never
aim for shit.

70
00:04:22,888 --> 00:04:24,595
Always collateral damage.

71
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:26,888
[both grunting]

72
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:29,216
You try to say
your last words.

73
00:04:29,311 --> 00:04:31,052
Project Sentry isn't
what she thinks.

74
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:32,887
But you start to fall asleep.

75
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,142
[yelps]

76
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,313
[gunshot]

77
00:04:36,026 --> 00:04:37,016
Oh...

78
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,355
[sighs]

79
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,611
Oh, damn.

80
00:04:42,658 --> 00:04:44,399
I needed that face.

81
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,742
Okay.

82
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:49,786
The assignment is--
Oh, wait. Hang on.

83
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:53,328
[crowd screams]

84
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:56,672
Assignment is complete.

85
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,212
What's next?

86
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,093
[reporter]
Representative Barnes,

87
00:05:09,184 --> 00:05:11,551
as a freshman congressman,
any words on today's hearing?

88
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:14,103
Well, I'm not
on the impeachment committee,

89
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:18,979
but the rumors of wrongdoing
are, um, very worrying.

90
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:23,529
They are, uh, very,
very concerning and worrying.

91
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:24,776
And, uh, I think that

92
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,948
my Brooklyn constituents
deserve better,

93
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,117
so we're-we're gonna get
to the bottom of this,

94
00:05:29,204 --> 00:05:32,822
um... [clears throat]
...worrying issue.

95
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:34,365
Thank you.

96
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:36,325
[reporters clamoring]

97
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:37,581
[gavel banging]

98
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:40,038
[congressman] Now, today,
the committee is meeting

99
00:05:40,132 --> 00:05:42,794
to examine this official
who sits before you.

100
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:46,297
Articles of impeachment
have been brought against her.

101
00:05:46,388 --> 00:05:49,380
And when we vote
in favor of the impeachment,

102
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:51,852
she will be removed
from her post permanently.

103
00:05:51,935 --> 00:05:53,846
Please state your name
for the record.

104
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:57,146
Valentina Allegra de Fontaine.

105
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,734
Mm-hmm.

106
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:00,808
- Uh, Miss Fontaine--
- [Valentina] No.

107
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:04,065
It's "de Fontaine."
You forgot the "de.”

108
00:06:04,156 --> 00:06:06,238
Mr. Anderson, for example,

109
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:10,613
is Secretary of Defense,
not secretary of "fense.”

110
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:11,694
[attendees chuckle]

111
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,779
[congressman]
Miss de Fontaine.

112
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:15,785
At this moment,
you are serving

113
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:17,492
as a director of the CIA,
correct?

114
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:18,792
That is correct.

115
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:20,961
And before that, you were
the chairwoman of the board

116
00:06:21,048 --> 00:06:22,334
of OXE Group?

117
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:25,587
Yes. Although, I have fully
divested in OXE

118
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:27,088
since taking office.

119
00:06:27,179 --> 00:06:31,047
I now sit on the board in
a strategic guidance capacity.

120
00:06:31,141 --> 00:06:34,930
And following
this strategic guidance,

121
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:37,432
the OXE Group
maintains significant holdings

122
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:40,310
in unregulated labs
in foreign countries

123
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,778
and rumored
human experimentation.

124
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:45,444
All part
of an illegal operation

125
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:49,865
to develop your own
super... person.

126
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,943
May I speak now, Congressman?

127
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:54,654
Yes.

128
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:56,659
First of all,
I don't have time

129
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:59,868
to entertain these rumors
and this gossip.

130
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:03,090
Right now, there are
multiple rogue nations

131
00:07:03,173 --> 00:07:06,416
with technologies
that far exceed our own.

132
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:09,172
And you'll recall that
our last president turned into

133
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:12,220
a bright red
superhuman monster

134
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:14,264
who nearly
destroyed this city.

135
00:07:16,812 --> 00:07:20,225
The Avengers are not
walking through that door.

136
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:23,728
We have no reliable heroes.

137
00:07:23,819 --> 00:07:27,778
That is why
the onus is on me, on us,

138
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:31,277
the American government,
to shield its citizens.

139
00:07:31,368 --> 00:07:32,574
- And you know...
- [gavel bangs]

140
00:07:32,661 --> 00:07:33,651
Madame Director.

141
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:35,327
...anything I have done
in my roles,

142
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:37,450
both at OXE or at the CIA,

143
00:07:37,541 --> 00:07:40,784
has been done
with that goal in mind.

144
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:42,663
- [gavel bangs]
- Order. Madame Director.

145
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:45,963
I officially reject
these articles of impeachment.

146
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:48,791
This is a partisan
waste of time.

147
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,262
And your hunt
will come up empty,

148
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:53,053
no matter how many
nooks and crannies

149
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,881
you happen
to stick your nose in.

150
00:07:54,975 --> 00:07:56,090
So you don't mind

151
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:59,017
if this committee continues
this investigation?

152
00:07:59,104 --> 00:08:00,845
Oh, of course not.

153
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:04,143
Shit.

154
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:06,271
We gotta get all of this
outta here ASAP.

155
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:08,443
Yep. So far they've removed
all the case studies...

156
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:10,646
Okay, just get rid
of any hanging chads

157
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,448
that could get me impeached
or land me in federal prison.

158
00:08:13,535 --> 00:08:14,991
Copy. No prison.

159
00:08:15,078 --> 00:08:17,490
[Valentina] What about our shadow ops
out in the field?

160
00:08:17,581 --> 00:08:19,037
Did all those loose ends
get tied up?

161
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:22,082
Well, the ends are tied, yes,
but the rope is on fire.

162
00:08:22,169 --> 00:08:23,330
What?

163
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,787
Can you please
just say it normal?

164
00:08:25,881 --> 00:08:28,714
Okay, um, one operative
blew up an entire laboratory

165
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,131
in the middle of Kuala Lumpur.

166
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,208
Whatever.

167
00:08:31,303 --> 00:08:33,089
Did the new assignments
get sent out?

168
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:35,217
Yes, ma'am.
All but one have checked in.

169
00:08:37,184 --> 00:08:38,265
Where is she?

170
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,142
[viewer laughing, chewing]

171
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,972
There's Brezhnev.

172
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,443
Those guys
with the little waves.

173
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,483
Get out of my way.

174
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:50,527
- Get out of my--
- [doorbell rings]

175
00:08:50,614 --> 00:08:52,981
I click "leave on porch."”

176
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,576
[doorbell rings]

177
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:58,698
Your "subordinance" will
be reported to DoorDash HQ.

178
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,654
[Yelena]
Alexei, it's me. Open up.

179
00:09:03,919 --> 00:09:05,000
Yelena?

180
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:08,704
Hold on!

181
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:21,645
[sighs]

182
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:25,520
"Protecting you
from boring evening."

183
00:09:26,358 --> 00:09:27,814
- Hmm.
- [door opens]

184
00:09:28,652 --> 00:09:31,360
Yelena! So good to see you.

185
00:09:32,697 --> 00:09:34,074
Hi, Dad.

186
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:36,068
Sorry for the wait.

187
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:38,696
I was on important call.

188
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:40,027
Highly classified.

189
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:43,747
How long has it been, huh?
A year?

190
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:47,993
Wow, yeah, I guess--
I guess it has been.

191
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,796
You-- You've been busy
with work?

192
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:53,339
Oh, yeah.

193
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:57,090
Yeah, a lot of, uh...
a lot of work.

194
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:59,842
- Me too.
- Too many irons in fire.

195
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:01,719
Uh, security.

196
00:10:02,644 --> 00:10:04,134
My limo business.

197
00:10:04,229 --> 00:10:05,970
You would not believe
the important people

198
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,395
I meet driving. [chuckles]

199
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,819
So you... you feel fulfilled?

200
00:10:10,902 --> 00:10:12,279
Oh, yeah.

201
00:10:12,362 --> 00:10:14,820
Yeah, so full, so filled.

202
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:17,819
Move to DC,
best decision I ever made.

203
00:10:17,909 --> 00:10:19,570
Isn't this technically
Baltimore?

204
00:10:19,661 --> 00:10:21,993
No. Baltimore start
next block over.

205
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,866
- Oh.
- But why do you ask this?

206
00:10:23,957 --> 00:10:26,915
What, uh--
What brings you here?

207
00:10:27,002 --> 00:10:32,623
Uh, |-- I wanted to talk
to you about Valentina.

208
00:10:32,716 --> 00:10:36,505
[chuckling] Okay.
New assignment.

209
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:38,756
You come to Red Guardian.
You want a little help.

210
00:10:38,847 --> 00:10:42,306
Uh, no, I--
I think I'm gonna quit.

211
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:43,632
What?

212
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:47,720
I would burn the city
to the ground to work for her.

213
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:50,146
What? You just said
you were fulfilled.

214
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:51,223
Lena, I was lying.

215
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:52,353
Look around you.
I'm miserable.

216
00:10:52,444 --> 00:10:53,559
Give me her number.

217
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,939
- No way.
- Give to me.

218
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:57,192
- Alexei, stop, stop.
- I call her. I use--

219
00:10:58,408 --> 00:10:59,648
Lena!

220
00:10:59,743 --> 00:11:01,700
Lena, what is wrong?

221
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:03,993
The light inside you is dim

222
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,866
even by
Eastern European standards.

223
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:08,953
I've just been wondering,
you know,

224
00:11:09,044 --> 00:11:13,288
like, what... is the point?

225
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,423
In any of this?

226
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:19,342
The point of work
is fame and fortune.

227
00:11:20,347 --> 00:11:22,588
Fortune buys friends,
and love,

228
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:25,219
and a lot of cool clothes.

229
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:26,971
- Okay. Thank you.
- Okay, okay--

230
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:28,552
- No, never mind. It's fine.
- No, no, no. Okay.

231
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:31,138
You-You want to know
when I was really happy?

232
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:32,768
Yes, please.

233
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:39,070
When I was serving my country
as a hero.

234
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:42,695
Saving civilians in streets.

235
00:11:42,786 --> 00:11:44,948
Being cheered on by the crowd.

236
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:47,370
Adored like a god.

237
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:50,074
[speaking Russian]

238
00:11:51,336 --> 00:11:53,327
There is no higher calling.

239
00:11:55,924 --> 00:11:58,291
Your sister understood
something about that.

240
00:11:58,385 --> 00:11:59,625
Mm-mmm.

241
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:03,053
Perhaps it is time
that you followed in her path.

242
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:08,554
Why do you have
this photo out?

243
00:12:14,109 --> 00:12:15,816
We were so bad.

244
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:18,230
You were happy.

245
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,567
I'll make you something.

246
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:27,778
You know, I'm still
super soldier in his prime.

247
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,454
Maybe you could
put in a good word

248
00:12:29,541 --> 00:12:32,954
with Valentina for me, huh?

249
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:38,039
Okay, Val. Reporting for duty.
What's my next assignment?

250
00:12:38,133 --> 00:12:40,795
Thank you, Ms. Belova.
I was starting to worry.

251
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:43,752
After this though,
I-- I need a change.

252
00:12:43,847 --> 00:12:44,962
[Valentina] <i>Oh, really?</i>

253
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:49,425
Yeah, maybe something
more public facing.

254
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:50,680
Interesting.

255
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,852
Yelena's ready
for her close-up?

256
00:12:52,939 --> 00:12:54,270
[chuckles]

257
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:57,145
Yeah, this just
isn't working for me anymore.

258
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:58,600
[Valentina sighs] <i>Okay, well,</i>

259
00:12:58,695 --> 00:13:00,527
<i>you know I love
promoting women.</i>

260
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:03,776
You complete this
last assignment for OXE,

261
00:13:03,867 --> 00:13:04,948
and you have a deal.

262
00:13:06,202 --> 00:13:07,192
<i>Okay?</i>

263
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:09,945
Okay.

264
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,074
[Valentina]
<i>There's a warehouse facility,</i>

265
00:13:14,169 --> 00:13:17,833
<i>a vault, built a mile down
into a mountain.</i>

266
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:22,462
<i>It stores all of OXE Group's
most sensitive assets.</i>

267
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:24,714
<i>Intel's come in
that a rogue operative</i>

268
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:27,045
<i>with attributes
perfectly tailored to rob me</i>

269
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:32,135
<i>is intending to...
well, rob me.</i>

270
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:34,435
I need you
to follow the target inside

271
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:38,106
<i>and find out
what she intends to steal.</i>

272
00:13:38,193 --> 00:13:40,480
<i>I'll add your biometrics
to the system.</i>

273
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,026
<i>You'll have full access.</i>

274
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:44,445
- [alarm blares]
- [door hisses]

275
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:46,398
<i>Once you assess
what's being stolen,</i>

276
00:13:46,493 --> 00:13:48,985
<i>you have the go-ahead
to terminate on sight.</i>

277
00:13:50,622 --> 00:13:51,783
<i>And then, no problem.</i>

278
00:13:51,873 --> 00:13:53,955
<i>You know, we can find you
some "good guy” material.</i>

279
00:13:59,172 --> 00:14:01,539
<i>It's simple, really.
It's just one little target...</i>

280
00:14:02,509 --> 00:14:03,499
<i>and you're done.</i>

281
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,369
[both grunting]

282
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:22,452
What is happening?

283
00:15:29,387 --> 00:15:30,923
You're not even my target.

284
00:15:31,014 --> 00:15:32,095
You're mine.

285
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:58,871
I'm not here for you.

286
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:18,725
[sighs] There you are.

287
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:20,518
Now what?

288
00:16:20,605 --> 00:16:22,312
[Ava] <i>Oh, get over yourself.</i>

289
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,485
[Yelena shouts]

290
00:16:39,457 --> 00:16:41,073
[Ava] <i>Stay out of my way.</i>

291
00:16:43,586 --> 00:16:44,576
[Walker groans]

292
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:19,865
[both straining]

293
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:38,259
[gun fires]

294
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:47,180
[stranger retching]

295
00:17:59,579 --> 00:18:01,570
[stranger groaning]

296
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:04,531
Is she actually dead? Oh...

297
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:16,801
Whoa. No. Hi. Hey. [chuckles]

298
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,008
[stammering] I'm-- I'm Bob.

299
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:23,557
[♪ jazz music playing]

300
00:18:23,561 --> 00:18:23,641
[♪ jazz music playing]

301
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,226
[♪ jazz music playing]

302
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:31,024
[Valentina] Yes, these are
the Chitauri handcuffs.

303
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,851
Recovered from
the Battle of New York

304
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,231
by the first responders.

305
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:35,812
They came
with the new property.

306
00:18:35,907 --> 00:18:38,399
Just reminds us that,
of course, we struggle,

307
00:18:38,493 --> 00:18:39,858
but then we get back up.

308
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,909
- Yes, we do.
- I love it. Yeah.

309
00:18:41,996 --> 00:18:43,657
- That's inspiring.
- Oh. [chuckles]

310
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,746
Thank you, Congressman.

311
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,699
I'm so happy that you're here.

312
00:18:47,794 --> 00:18:50,456
Yes, this is
a beautiful fake event, Val.

313
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:53,079
"The First Responders
Family Fund."

314
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:54,881
- Yes.
- That's cute.

315
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,503
Cute? Oh.

316
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,426
This won't sway the votes
enough to save your ass.

317
00:18:58,513 --> 00:19:00,550
Oh. [chuckles]

318
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:03,423
Okay. So, can you go
get him, Mel?

319
00:19:03,518 --> 00:19:04,633
- Yep.
- Thank you.

320
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:08,766
This gaudy Avenger propaganda
reeks of desperation.

321
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:11,598
If you really thought that,
you wouldn't be here.

322
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:12,853
You're scared

323
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:16,107
because your investigation
of my office came up clean.

324
00:19:16,197 --> 00:19:18,108
- Hmm. Squeaky clean.
- Mm-hmm.

325
00:19:18,199 --> 00:19:20,691
Almost like someone
had frantically gotten rid

326
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:21,775
of all the evidence.

327
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:24,327
Or like someone
was incredibly innocent.

328
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:25,665
Without proof,

329
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:28,331
this impeachment thing
IS running on borrowed time.

330
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,623
[photographer] Uh, excuse me.

331
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:30,700
Turn around.

332
00:19:31,462 --> 00:19:32,964
Oh. [laughs]

333
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:34,549
- How great.
- Oh, thank you.

334
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:36,418
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you very much.

335
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:37,544
Ah...

336
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:43,850
What do you think?

337
00:19:43,933 --> 00:19:44,968
Oh.

338
00:19:45,977 --> 00:19:47,058
- Hi.
- Mel, right?

339
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:48,885
- Mm-hmm.
- Mmm.

340
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:51,267
This must all seem like
ancient history to you.

341
00:19:52,942 --> 00:19:54,524
You know, Kierkegaard says

342
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:57,068
that life can only
be understood backwards.

343
00:19:58,322 --> 00:20:00,063
- Very true.
- Is it?

344
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:01,898
I don't know, actually.

345
00:20:01,993 --> 00:20:03,324
It did sound good, though.

346
00:20:03,411 --> 00:20:05,368
He did believe that
it was up to individuals

347
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,365
- to create values.
- Hmm.

348
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,952
I know who you are
and what you're doing.

349
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,332
What am I doing?

350
00:20:15,423 --> 00:20:16,788
You're working me.

351
00:20:16,883 --> 00:20:18,715
You're trying to get me
on your side.

352
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:22,005
Okay, look. I...

353
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:23,837
Y-You say you know who I am.

354
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:25,137
So you know my story,

355
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:28,387
and you know I didn't have
a choice who I worked for.

356
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:30,468
But you do.

357
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,647
I need to keep Valentina
on schedule.

358
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,190
[sighs] Oh.

359
00:20:36,277 --> 00:20:38,359
What is this? This your trash?

360
00:20:38,446 --> 00:20:40,778
- It's my business card.
- Oh.

361
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:42,731
In case you need some help or,

362
00:20:42,825 --> 00:20:45,283
you know, you wanna share
some secret hidden evidence.

363
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:46,530
Ah.

364
00:20:46,621 --> 00:20:48,077
Okay. Goodbye.

365
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,079
Who are you?

366
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:56,081
I'm-- I'm Bob. I told you.
I'm, uh...

367
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:58,295
Yeah. [chuckles] Bob.

368
00:20:58,382 --> 00:20:59,713
Jesus Christ.
Stop saying "Bob."

369
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,302
- Who sent you, Bob?
- [Bob] Nobody.

370
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:03,342
Why would I be sent?

371
00:21:03,429 --> 00:21:04,794
Were you all--
You were all sent?

372
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:06,721
[Ava] Okay, I'm not sure
what's happening here,

373
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:08,468
but you're all exhausting
and my job is done, so--

374
00:21:08,559 --> 00:21:11,301
Ah, but you see my job
is to keep an eye on you.

375
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:13,306
So, no, you are not gonna go
anywhere anymore.

376
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:15,354
So you're keeping
an eye on her, huh?

377
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:16,647
That's a halfway decent cover

378
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:18,475
for somebody stealing assets
from OXE.

379
00:21:18,569 --> 00:21:20,947
I'm not stealing.
She's stealing.

380
00:21:25,576 --> 00:21:26,691
[sighs]

381
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:29,694
Okay.

382
00:21:30,748 --> 00:21:33,615
It's clear we have all
worked for Valentina

383
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:35,871
in some sort of
shadow ops capacity.

384
00:21:35,962 --> 00:21:37,544
Yeah. So?

385
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:39,462
So all of this stuff
is OXE's secrets.

386
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:40,754
But so are we.

387
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:43,629
Which makes us liabilities
that no one would miss.

388
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:44,971
Oh, speak for yourself.

389
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,546
We are the evidence,
and this is the shredder.

390
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,130
She wants us gone.

391
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:50,590
Your theory's flawed.

392
00:21:50,685 --> 00:21:52,392
Oh, please. Go on.

393
00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:54,845
Okay. Well, look at the facts.

394
00:21:54,939 --> 00:21:56,600
The infamous Ghost.

395
00:21:56,691 --> 00:21:59,103
A SHIELD reject on the run
from 15 nations?

396
00:21:59,193 --> 00:22:00,308
'Cause the dead one
over there,

397
00:22:00,403 --> 00:22:01,564
she destroyed
half of Budapest.

398
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,770
Don't talk about her
like that.

399
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,446
And you,
former Red Room assassin.

400
00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:07,524
God only knows
the blood on your hands.

401
00:22:07,618 --> 00:22:08,608
Pretty ludicrous

402
00:22:08,703 --> 00:22:10,410
coming from the dime-store
Captain America.

403
00:22:10,496 --> 00:22:11,657
I'll have you know
I was actually

404
00:22:11,747 --> 00:22:13,078
the official Captain America,
SO...

405
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:14,906
[scoffs]
Yeah, for, like, two seconds.

406
00:22:15,001 --> 00:22:16,332
Before you publicly murdered
an innocent man

407
00:22:16,419 --> 00:22:17,534
on the streets.

408
00:22:17,628 --> 00:22:19,744
- Do I have that right?
- Really? Define "innocent.”

409
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:22,422
Hey, look. I'm a decorated
combat veteran, okay?

410
00:22:22,508 --> 00:22:24,215
I have a loving wife
and a son.

411
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:27,043
Let's be honest, you guys are
just cheap mercenaries. Okay?

412
00:22:27,138 --> 00:22:29,175
So, I-- Clearly, I'm supposed
to bring you in.

413
00:22:29,265 --> 00:22:30,380
[both laughing]

414
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:32,761
That was funny.
Thank you. We needed that.

415
00:22:32,852 --> 00:22:35,093
[Bob laughs]

416
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:38,430
It was getting so tense
in here for a second.

417
00:22:38,524 --> 00:22:39,514
[clears throat]

418
00:22:41,068 --> 00:22:43,685
I'm not leaving here
without completing my mission.

419
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:46,111
Valentina gave me
a clean slate guarantee,

420
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:47,484
and I'm not screwing that up.

421
00:22:47,575 --> 00:22:51,239
But this weirdo wasn't part
of the job, so I gotta know...

422
00:22:53,914 --> 00:22:54,995
How'd you get in?

423
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,538
[sighs]

424
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:58,036
I don't-- I don't remember.

425
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:02,078
Terrific answer.

426
00:23:02,173 --> 00:23:04,505
All right, um...
Tie yourselves up.

427
00:23:04,592 --> 00:23:06,924
- Wow. No.
- Oh, my God.

428
00:23:07,011 --> 00:23:08,342
And goodbye.

429
00:23:14,393 --> 00:23:16,475
- [high-pitched buzzing]
- [exclaims]

430
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:22,265
[buzzing stops]

431
00:23:22,359 --> 00:23:24,396
[pants]

432
00:23:25,196 --> 00:23:26,357
[groans]

433
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,492
You guys hear that?

434
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,653
Isn't that amazing? Cheers.

435
00:23:35,748 --> 00:23:37,614
And she said,
"Not on my watch."

436
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:39,699
[♪ jazz music playing]

437
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:45,587
- Congressman Gary.
- Hey!

438
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:47,051
I have a plan.

439
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:48,295
Holy shit, Bucky.

440
00:23:49,887 --> 00:23:51,878
The assistant, she's ductile.

441
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:54,634
- Ductile? Oh.
- Yeah.

442
00:23:54,725 --> 00:23:55,760
I-I mean, good.

443
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:57,307
But next time,
why don't you just text me

444
00:23:57,394 --> 00:23:58,520
like a normal person?

445
00:23:58,604 --> 00:24:00,561
Look, we're safe here.
We're in a blind spot, okay?

446
00:24:00,648 --> 00:24:01,934
Away from those two cameras.

447
00:24:02,024 --> 00:24:03,640
Just hold on, all right?

448
00:24:03,734 --> 00:24:06,351
We don't need to go rogue
in the darkness,

449
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:07,526
or whatever you people do.

450
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:09,524
Hold on”? You don't know
what Val is capable of.

451
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:10,776
We need to move fast,

452
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:12,482
and the assistant
is on the fence.

453
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:13,862
Without a smoking gun,

454
00:24:13,953 --> 00:24:17,287
the best chance to get Val out
of power is to whip the votes.

455
00:24:17,373 --> 00:24:18,454
And you can help with that

456
00:24:18,541 --> 00:24:20,373
and then let the system
do its job.

457
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:22,951
The system that goes on recess
every day at 4:00 p.m.

458
00:24:23,045 --> 00:24:25,377
We are in a good spot,
I assure you.

459
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:27,922
My team is putting together
a juicy packet

460
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:28,998
for the next hearing.

461
00:24:29,969 --> 00:24:32,131
- Packet?
- Yes, Bucky.

462
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:34,052
Read the packets.

463
00:24:39,395 --> 00:24:40,681
Is it time?

464
00:24:40,771 --> 00:24:43,854
I can confirm all your
"guests" are in attendance,

465
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:46,854
and vault level five has been
completely sealed off.

466
00:24:46,944 --> 00:24:47,934
All right, then.

467
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:53,194
"All right, then. Move on
to the final step"? Or...

468
00:24:53,284 --> 00:24:54,570
Torch it all.

469
00:24:55,077 --> 00:24:56,238
Right. Um...

470
00:24:57,496 --> 00:24:59,362
- Are you-- Are you sure?
- Oh, my God.

471
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:01,747
[Yelena] Hey.

472
00:25:01,834 --> 00:25:04,667
Job or not, can you have
some respect, please?

473
00:25:04,753 --> 00:25:06,039
Yeah, Jesus.

474
00:25:07,006 --> 00:25:08,087
Hold on a second.

475
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:11,169
What? She'd want me
to have it. [chuckles]

476
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:12,667
I need it.

477
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:14,377
[alarm blaring]

478
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:16,925
[mechanical hissing, whirring]

479
00:25:17,016 --> 00:25:18,177
What the hell is that?

480
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,883
That doesn't sound
like a shredder.

481
00:25:20,728 --> 00:25:22,139
It's an incinerator.

482
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,857
Two minutes.

483
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:26,977
Then Valentina's slate
Is wiped clean.

484
00:25:27,067 --> 00:25:29,058
You don't know that for sure.
Could be for anything.

485
00:25:29,153 --> 00:25:30,643
Could be for when they come
to pick me up.

486
00:25:30,738 --> 00:25:31,944
[Ava] Do you feel that?

487
00:25:32,031 --> 00:25:34,193
The temperature rising
dramatically

488
00:25:34,283 --> 00:25:35,614
as if heat was involved?

489
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,156
Okay, it's an incinerator.

490
00:25:39,246 --> 00:25:41,283
Oh, boy. That is no way to go.

491
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:42,875
Well, how would you
like to die today, Bob?

492
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:43,993
Okay, ghost lady.

493
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,700
- Ava.
- Sure. Whatever. Don't care.

494
00:25:45,794 --> 00:25:47,046
We need to get you
through the walls,

495
00:25:47,129 --> 00:25:48,164
so that you can open the door.

496
00:25:48,255 --> 00:25:50,667
- She tried that already.
- I know she did.

497
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:52,374
But we haven't tried shutting
down the sound barrier.

498
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:56,006
Well, if they built it
just for her,

499
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:58,224
there's gotta be
an independent power source.

500
00:25:59,141 --> 00:26:00,723
[Ava] Come on. Let's go.

501
00:26:04,188 --> 00:26:05,724
What-- What exactly
are we looking for?

502
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:08,021
We're looking for
not-stupid questions, Bob.

503
00:26:21,622 --> 00:26:22,862
[Yelena] I think I found it.

504
00:26:24,041 --> 00:26:25,076
Move!

505
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:29,376
I can override this.

506
00:26:29,463 --> 00:26:30,453
On your left!

507
00:26:32,508 --> 00:26:33,498
Or that works, I hope.

508
00:26:33,592 --> 00:26:35,003
Go, go, go.

509
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:51,019
You think she's coming back?

510
00:26:52,278 --> 00:26:54,269
I should have
seen this coming.

511
00:27:09,962 --> 00:27:11,953
- [alarm blares]
- [door hisses]

512
00:27:23,142 --> 00:27:24,632
[child] Yelena!

513
00:27:27,688 --> 00:27:29,019
Yelena!

514
