okay?

771
00:38:58,753 --> 00:38:59,743
Somebody's got to go first.

772
00:38:59,838 --> 00:39:01,454
Cucumber, cucumber, cucumber.

773
00:39:01,548 --> 00:39:02,709
What the hell is happening?

774
00:39:02,799 --> 00:39:04,381
Growing up, somebody told me
that you can stop a sneeze

775
00:39:04,467 --> 00:39:05,457
if you confuse your brain.

776
00:39:05,552 --> 00:39:06,587
I always just yelled
"cucumber.”

777
00:39:06,678 --> 00:39:07,793
- Okay.
- I have to sneeze.

778
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:09,753
But if I sneeze, then
I'm going to lose control.

779
00:39:09,848 --> 00:39:11,964
This is insane, okay?
I can get us all out of here.

780
00:39:12,058 --> 00:39:13,093
- I just need to go first.
- No.

781
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:14,174
There's got to be another way.

782
00:39:14,269 --> 00:39:16,476
[exhales] Oh, no.

783
00:39:16,563 --> 00:39:18,645
- Cucumber! Cucumber!
- Cucumber! Cucumber!

784
00:39:18,732 --> 00:39:21,269
All right! Come on! Okay,
just give me this. I got it!

785
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:22,895
[all shouting]

786
00:39:25,697 --> 00:39:26,983
[grunts]

787
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:29,443
[grunts, pants]

788
00:39:31,911 --> 00:39:33,322
[sneezes]

789
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,622
You selfish prick.

790
00:39:37,709 --> 00:39:39,416
Yet, you're all safe.

791
00:39:39,502 --> 00:39:41,163
I made a tactical decision

792
00:39:41,254 --> 00:39:43,666
to secure my own safety
and ensure all yours.

793
00:39:45,216 --> 00:39:47,378
Pretty ungrateful
if you ask me, but...

794
00:39:47,469 --> 00:39:48,459
You gonna make it, Bobby?

795
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:53,672
Looks like you might have
missed arm, leg and chest day.

796
00:40:02,901 --> 00:40:04,062
[baby fusses]

797
00:40:04,152 --> 00:40:06,143
- [Olivia] John?
- What?

798
00:40:08,031 --> 00:40:09,817
[Olivia] Are you watching him?

799
00:40:09,908 --> 00:40:12,070
What? I'm doing it.
I'm watching him.

800
00:40:14,871 --> 00:40:16,236
[baby cries]

801
00:40:23,838 --> 00:40:25,499
- John.
- What, Olivia? What?

802
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:27,752
- Please.
- I'm watching him. He's fine.

803
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:28,877
You're in your phone.

804
00:40:30,053 --> 00:40:32,010
Look, you don't like
the way that I do it,

805
00:40:32,097 --> 00:40:33,929
then you can do it yourself,
okay?

806
00:40:34,015 --> 00:40:36,131
[baby crying]

807
00:40:39,938 --> 00:40:42,179
It's okay. It's okay.

808
00:40:46,486 --> 00:40:47,476
[Yelena] <i>Walker.</i>

809
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:50,482
Uh...

810
00:40:50,573 --> 00:40:51,859
What the hell are you doing?

811
00:41:01,251 --> 00:41:02,707
I'm fine.

812
00:41:05,964 --> 00:41:07,546
[Ava] All right,
let's get out of here.

813
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:13,718
[people clamoring]

814
00:41:26,526 --> 00:41:27,732
[Yelena] Okay, we need
to come up with a plan.

815
00:41:27,819 --> 00:41:29,685
- [Walker] Here's what we're gonna do.
- You're the boss now? Cute.

816
00:41:29,779 --> 00:41:31,861
Yeah, it's our only chance
of getting out of here, so...

817
00:41:31,948 --> 00:41:33,905
Okay, I think I might
just surrender, probably.

818
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:35,323
Okay, fine.
Every man for himself.

819
00:41:35,410 --> 00:41:36,571
Why should you be in charge?

820
00:41:36,661 --> 00:41:38,368
You almost killed all of us
right there.

821
00:41:38,454 --> 00:41:40,195
Well, let's see.
I've been in the trenches

822
00:41:40,290 --> 00:41:41,951
of every war-torn country
on this planet,

823
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:43,543
rescued God knows
how many hostages

824
00:41:43,626 --> 00:41:45,412
and shook the hands
of two US presidents.

825
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:46,743
What else? Uh...

826
00:41:46,838 --> 00:41:49,671
Oh, high school state football
champs back-to-back-to-back.

827
00:41:49,757 --> 00:41:51,668
- Go Bears.
- Oh, wow.

828
00:41:51,759 --> 00:41:53,841
When I was five,
I was in a peewee soccer team

829
00:41:53,928 --> 00:41:55,635
called the West Chesapeake
Valley Thunderbolts

830
00:41:55,722 --> 00:41:57,258
sponsored by
Shane's Tire Shop.

831
00:41:57,348 --> 00:41:58,338
We won zero games,

832
00:41:58,433 --> 00:41:59,719
and one time,
this girl, Mindy,

833
00:41:59,809 --> 00:42:01,015
she did a poo at midfield.

834
00:42:01,102 --> 00:42:04,265
Anyone else have any pointless
childhood stories to tell?

835
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:06,221
Grew up in a lab prison.

836
00:42:06,316 --> 00:42:08,728
Meth-addicted
sign-twirling chicken.

837
00:42:08,818 --> 00:42:10,980
It was a summer job.

838
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:12,276
Right. Okay, here's the plan.

839
00:42:12,363 --> 00:42:14,775
We set off an explosion
to bring them in.

840
00:42:14,866 --> 00:42:16,698
No. Too many variables
with an explosion.

841
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:17,945
They turn on
their night vision.

842
00:42:18,036 --> 00:42:19,902
You handle the first wave,
but you wait for me

843
00:42:19,996 --> 00:42:21,452
after I've blinded
the remaining troops.

844
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:24,122
- I'm just going to wait for ya?
- It will only work if you wait.

845
00:42:24,209 --> 00:42:25,199
[Walker] Terrible plan.

846
00:42:25,293 --> 00:42:26,408
- Ava, you...
- [Ava's suit activates]

847
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:27,628
...find an escape vehicle.

848
00:42:31,216 --> 00:42:32,331
Uh, what about me?

849
00:42:34,010 --> 00:42:36,377
You stay behind me, Bob.

850
00:42:38,014 --> 00:42:39,220
[sighs]

851
00:42:39,307 --> 00:42:40,718
Let's do this.

852
00:42:45,855 --> 00:42:47,016
[Valentina] What's the latest?

853
00:42:47,774 --> 00:42:48,764
We're dug in, ma'am.

854
00:42:48,858 --> 00:42:50,394
Got it covered
from all angles.

855
00:42:50,485 --> 00:42:51,941
There's no way out.

856
00:42:52,028 --> 00:42:53,564
Breach team ready
at the front.

857
00:42:53,655 --> 00:42:55,896
It's going to be
non-lethal protocol.

858
00:42:55,990 --> 00:42:58,732
Non-lethal? No one told me
this was non-lethal.

859
00:42:58,826 --> 00:43:00,328
Well, I'm telling you now,
Holt.

860
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:02,027
It's just...

861
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:04,249
I've spent a lot of time
planning for lethal.

862
00:43:04,332 --> 00:43:06,243
Then change the plan. Okay?

863
00:43:06,334 --> 00:43:07,369
There's somebody inside there

864
00:43:07,460 --> 00:43:08,666
I don't want
catching any strays.

865
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:10,501
[agent] Get down!

866
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:14,797
Strike Team 4, enter now.

867
00:43:14,884 --> 00:43:16,170
Non-lethal.

868
00:43:35,571 --> 00:43:37,482
In one minute,
these all go back on.

869
00:43:38,616 --> 00:43:39,993
Okay.

870
00:43:40,076 --> 00:43:41,407
Maybe I should have a gun?

871
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:42,996
Hmm. No, I don't think so.

872
00:43:43,079 --> 00:43:44,194
But we are gonna need--

873
00:43:44,289 --> 00:43:45,905
We're gonna need
to fight, right? So...

874
00:43:45,999 --> 00:43:47,910
Mm-hmm. I will fight.
You stay behind me.

875
00:43:49,669 --> 00:43:51,785
The medical trial was supposed
to make me better,

876
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:54,746
and, I don't know, I feel like
maybe I could help.

877
00:43:57,218 --> 00:44:00,802
I thought you said that you
didn't know anything about it.

878
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:03,346
No, not much. I just remember
they said it was for people

879
00:44:03,433 --> 00:44:06,676
who wanted to make something
better of themselves.

880
00:44:06,769 --> 00:44:07,759
Mmm.

881
00:44:07,854 --> 00:44:09,811
You can trust me, Bob.

882
00:44:11,190 --> 00:44:12,180
Can I?

883
00:44:13,568 --> 00:44:14,808
No, not really.

884
00:44:14,902 --> 00:44:16,404
[both chuckle]

885
00:44:19,449 --> 00:44:22,407
I-- I've always had these
episodes since I was a kid.

886
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:26,031
There's a... There's a high,
then there's a big low,

887
00:44:26,122 --> 00:44:28,454
and then my memory
just goes blank.

888
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:32,538
But this time,
I feel like there's...

889
00:44:32,628 --> 00:44:34,289
I don't know,
something bad happened

890
00:44:34,380 --> 00:44:35,370
or I did something bad.

891
00:44:35,465 --> 00:44:37,706
I mean, everyone here
has done bad things.

892
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:40,087
I think this was like
a whole new kind of--

893
00:44:40,178 --> 00:44:41,919
- [device beeps]
- Oh.

894
00:44:43,348 --> 00:44:44,338
Lights up.

895
00:44:47,602 --> 00:44:51,095
No. Why...
Why did that not work?

896
00:44:51,189 --> 00:44:53,100
Well, you got to turn
the power back on.

897
00:44:53,191 --> 00:44:54,556
I mean, you got to blind
the guys.

898
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:56,482
- Yeah, I know that, Bob.
- That was your plan.

899
00:44:56,569 --> 00:44:57,684
You're not being helpful, Bob.

900
00:44:57,779 --> 00:44:59,736
Give me that. Follow me.

901
00:44:59,822 --> 00:45:02,439
I hate to say it, but I think
Walter was right on this one.

902
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:04,399
His name is Walker, Bob.

903
00:45:06,662 --> 00:45:08,323
Turn on the lights, Yelena.

904
00:45:08,414 --> 00:45:10,792
[breathing heavily]

905
00:45:13,211 --> 00:45:14,542
I got to do everything myself.

906
00:45:14,629 --> 00:45:15,619
[grunts]

907
00:45:15,713 --> 00:45:16,953
[gunshots]

908
00:45:17,465 --> 00:45:19,126
[shushes]

909
00:45:22,387 --> 00:45:23,422
I will repeat,

910
00:45:23,513 --> 00:45:26,301
Tango Foxtrot Lima
requesting report.

911
00:45:29,018 --> 00:45:30,520
Next team up, get in there!

912
00:45:35,274 --> 00:45:36,810
- Where is he?
- He's gone.

913
00:45:37,777 --> 00:45:39,609
Every man for himself, right?

914
00:45:40,613 --> 00:45:42,149
- [Yelena] Shit.
- [Bob] Oh.

915
00:45:57,422 --> 00:45:58,628
[grunting]

916
00:45:58,714 --> 00:45:59,704
[Yelena] Get down!

917
00:45:59,799 --> 00:46:01,540
- [Bob] I can help.
- Stay behind me.

918
00:46:01,634 --> 00:46:02,999
[groans]

919
00:46:03,594 --> 00:46:04,846
Bob, stay!

920
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:10,507
That's it. You're done.

921
00:46:10,601 --> 00:46:12,103
No, wait! I can help!

922
00:46:17,775 --> 00:46:19,732
- Take this!
- Yes! How-- How do I use it?

923
00:46:19,819 --> 00:46:21,309
You point and shoot.

924
00:46:21,404 --> 00:46:22,394
Shit.

925
00:46:26,701 --> 00:46:29,033
- Sorry!
- A little higher!

926
00:46:32,665 --> 00:46:34,497
- That was awesome.
- Not at me!

927
00:46:35,251 --> 00:46:37,492
No! Stop! Stop shooting!

928
00:46:37,587 --> 00:46:40,045
Stop! Stop! It's me!
It's John! Stop!

929
00:46:40,131 --> 00:46:42,623
- Where were you?
- Where were you?

930
00:46:42,717 --> 00:46:44,003
The explosion fried the wires.

931
00:46:44,093 --> 00:46:46,130
I told you, too many variables.
I knew it.

932
00:46:46,220 --> 00:46:48,131
- And then, you didn't wait.
- I did wait! And the--

933
00:46:48,222 --> 00:46:49,883
[Holt on radio]
<i>What's going on in there?</i>

934
00:46:49,974 --> 00:46:51,135
<i>Do we need to go lethal?</i>

935
00:46:51,225 --> 00:46:53,262
- [radio beeps]
- Okay.

936
00:46:53,352 --> 00:46:54,683
We probably got
about 60 seconds

937
00:46:54,770 --> 00:46:56,147
until they mobilize.

938
00:46:56,230 --> 00:46:58,608
And if ghost lady actually did
what she was supposed to,

939
00:46:58,691 --> 00:47:00,898
maybe we'll all
get out of here alive.

940
00:47:08,910 --> 00:47:10,867
[Bob] I don't really want
to be carried anymore.

941
00:47:10,953 --> 00:47:13,490
[Walker] Shut up, Bob.
You're injured, remember?

942
00:47:28,179 --> 00:47:29,669
[Walker] We need a truck.

943
00:47:30,431 --> 00:47:31,933
[Yelena] Where's Ava?

944
00:47:32,016 --> 00:47:35,429
[Walker] She's gone.
Of course she's gone.

945
00:47:35,520 --> 00:47:36,885
[Bob] Now what?

946
00:47:37,772 --> 00:47:39,433
Hey! Get in.

947
00:47:42,568 --> 00:47:44,275
[Yelena] You going
to be okay back here?

948
00:47:44,362 --> 00:47:46,353
- Yeah. All good.
- Yeah? Okay.

949
00:47:51,285 --> 00:47:53,868
Second time you came back.
[chuckles]

950
00:47:53,955 --> 00:47:55,366
This was the only
way out, okay?

951
00:47:55,456 --> 00:47:57,618
- That's all.
- All right.

952
00:47:57,708 --> 00:47:59,870
[Walker] Oh, shit.

953
00:47:59,961 --> 00:48:01,827
All right. Just, uh,
let me do the talking, okay?

954
00:48:01,921 --> 00:48:03,707
- [Yelena] Oh, my God.
- Here we go.

955
00:48:09,053 --> 00:48:10,635
Identify yourself, soldiers.

956
00:48:10,721 --> 00:48:11,836
Part of the medical team.

957
00:48:11,931 --> 00:48:13,797
Need to get the wounded
to the hospital.

958
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:15,632
[agent] Medical bay's set up
north side.

959
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:17,228
[Walker] Nah,
medical bay won't suffice.

960
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:19,052
We were headed off-base.

961
00:48:19,146 --> 00:48:20,432
[agent]
No one leaves the premises

962
00:48:20,523 --> 00:48:22,139
until mission is completed.

963
00:48:22,233 --> 00:48:25,225
Orders are no deviations
from protocol.

964
00:48:25,319 --> 00:48:27,026
Identify yourself.

965
00:48:30,074 --> 00:48:32,611
- No.
- Oh, wow, masterful.

966
00:48:33,703 --> 00:48:36,161
Remove your helmets
and identify yourself.

967
00:48:36,247 --> 00:48:37,237
Now, soldiers!

968
00:48:37,331 --> 00:48:38,446
You are messing
with the wrong--

969
00:48:38,541 --> 00:48:39,576
[gunfire]

970
00:48:41,752 --> 00:48:43,004
[gunfire continues]

971
00:48:50,261 --> 00:48:51,422
[Bob] Hey!

972
00:48:52,680 --> 00:48:53,795
Over here!

973
00:48:56,142 --> 00:48:57,382
Move, move, move!

974
00:49:01,355 --> 00:49:02,766
Oh, no. Bob helped.

975
00:49:04,358 --> 00:49:07,225
Open fire. End this now.
I want him toes up.

976
00:49:07,320 --> 00:49:08,936
[guns fire]

977
00:49:13,868 --> 00:49:14,903
What the hell are you doing?

978
00:49:14,994 --> 00:49:16,200
This has gone far--
[yelps, chokes]

979
00:49:17,204 --> 00:49:19,070
Cease fire! Cease fire!

980
00:49:19,165 --> 00:49:20,781
[agent] Cease fire!

981
00:49:25,671 --> 00:49:26,661
[Ava] Come on. Let's go.

982
00:49:28,841 --> 00:49:30,878
Come on. Let's go.
That's why he did it.

983
00:49:45,816 --> 00:49:46,806
[agent] What the...

984
00:50:10,257 --> 00:50:11,634
[guns fire]

985
00:50:22,687 --> 00:50:23,802
Is that...

986
00:50:42,415 --> 00:50:45,032
Mel, I need you to connect me
to our satellites.

987
00:50:45,126 --> 00:50:48,289
I need to know exactly where
he's going, and I need it now.

988
00:50:48,379 --> 00:50:51,246
I, uh... I think he's coming
back down.

989
00:50:58,222 --> 00:51:01,590
- No. No, no, no.
- Oh, shit.

990
00:51:29,128 --> 00:51:30,414
[Ava grunts]

991
00:51:30,504 --> 00:51:31,960
[Walker] Oh, God.

992
00:51:32,840 --> 00:51:34,456
[Yelena] I'll call an Uber.

993
00:51:35,050 --> 00:51:36,211
Jesus Christ.

994
00:51:36,302 --> 00:51:38,043
I know. What was that?

995
00:51:38,137 --> 00:51:40,003
That was her.

996
00:51:40,097 --> 00:51:41,258
She did that to him.

997
00:51:41,348 --> 00:51:44,056
Well, she turned him into
a tomahawk cruise missile.

998
00:51:44,143 --> 00:51:47,352
You were right,
she definitely wants us dead.

999
00:51:47,438 --> 00:51:50,556
To test on someone like that,
it's inhuman.

1000
00:51:50,649 --> 00:51:51,810
Yeah, she's lost it.

1001
00:51:51,901 --> 00:51:53,983
Nope. She's found it.

1002
00:51:54,779 --> 00:51:56,361
And she'll use it.

1003
00:51:56,447 --> 00:51:57,562
What is this?

1004
00:51:58,783 --> 00:52:01,491
"Power of a thousand
exploding suns."

1005
00:52:01,577 --> 00:52:03,238
"Golden Guardian of Good."

1006
00:52:03,329 --> 00:52:04,569
That's a mouthful.

1007
00:52:06,415 --> 00:52:07,405
Wow.

1008
00:52:08,083 --> 00:52:09,744
Sentry.

1009
00:52:09,835 --> 00:52:11,417
Very shiny,
I'll give them that.

1010
00:52:11,504 --> 00:52:12,790
[Ava] And what do you know
about this?

1011
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:15,087
There was a rumor
that OXE was on the verge

1012
00:52:15,174 --> 00:52:16,960
of some kind
of big breakthrough.

1013
00:52:17,051 --> 00:52:18,883
Whatever it was
was way too extreme.

1014
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:20,425
Test subjects were dying.

1015
00:52:20,513 --> 00:52:21,548
When the government looked
into it,

1016
00:52:21,639 --> 00:52:22,629
Val shut it down.

1017
00:52:22,723 --> 00:52:25,010
She put me on cleanup duty.

1018
00:52:25,100 --> 00:52:27,683
Let's just make it home
without getting cratered.

1019
00:52:27,770 --> 00:52:28,976
Might need new homes.

1020
00:52:29,063 --> 00:52:30,178
Anybody hungry?

1021
00:52:31,607 --> 00:52:32,597
Cactus berry.

1022
00:52:34,151 --> 00:52:35,437
Let me see here.

1023
00:52:35,528 --> 00:52:38,065
So, um, that woman
back there that |I...

1024
00:52:40,783 --> 00:52:42,069
You knew her?

1025
00:52:43,369 --> 00:52:44,404
Yeah, I did.

1026
00:52:45,663 --> 00:52:47,574
She had a tough life.

1027
00:52:47,665 --> 00:52:49,906
She killed a lot of people,
and then she got killed.

1028
00:52:51,043 --> 00:52:52,329
Same as us someday.

1029
00:52:53,337 --> 00:52:54,623
It's a shit life.

1030
00:52:55,923 --> 00:52:57,163
Yeah, well...

1031
00:52:58,133 --> 00:53:00,295
what other life can we have?

1032
00:53:00,386 --> 00:53:02,844
[Ava] Says the guy with
the Norman Rockwell family

1033
00:53:02,930 --> 00:53:04,466
waiting for him at home.

1034
00:53:06,934 --> 00:53:08,095
Yeah.

1035
00:53:09,395 --> 00:53:10,601
How do you do it?

1036
00:53:13,148 --> 00:53:16,686
Well, you just keep working
at it every day.

1037
00:53:18,153 --> 00:53:19,279
Never give up.

1038
00:53:21,699 --> 00:53:22,734
Beautiful.

1039
00:53:24,118 --> 00:53:26,325
Dr. Phil,
that was really beautiful.

1040
00:53:29,248 --> 00:53:31,580
Yeah. You know that show's
not on anymore, right?

1041
00:53:31,667 --> 00:53:32,702
[Yelena]
Yeah, it is. I watch it.

1042
00:53:32,793 --> 00:53:34,830
[Walker] Nah, it got canceled
a few years ago.

1043
00:53:34,920 --> 00:53:36,661
It was a good show
while it was on,

1044
00:53:36,755 --> 00:53:38,041
but it's not on anymore.

1045
00:53:38,132 --> 00:53:40,920
Gotta be like a YouTube thing.
They took him off cable.

1046
00:53:42,177 --> 00:53:43,713
[Mel] Well, it isn't great.

1047
00:53:43,804 --> 00:53:44,794
Seven local outlets

1048
00:53:44,889 --> 00:53:46,630
have picked up
the story of the blast.

1049
00:53:46,724 --> 00:53:48,965
One has already connected
the vault to OXE.

1050
00:53:49,059 --> 00:53:51,642
And I have 15 messages
from concerned House members

1051
00:53:51,729 --> 00:53:53,311
on our side of the aisle.

1052
00:53:53,397 --> 00:53:54,808
[Valentina] You know,
I don't say it enough,

1053
00:53:54,899 --> 00:53:56,765
but I am so impressed

1054
00:53:56,859 --> 00:53:58,941
that in circumstances
like this,

1055
00:53:59,028 --> 00:54:01,565
you can still get me
a good cup of coffee.

1056
00:54:01,655 --> 00:54:03,362
It's extraordinary.

1057
00:54:03,991 --> 00:54:04,981
[Mel] Thank you.

1058
00:54:05,075 --> 00:54:06,361
[Valentina]
Okay, time to pivot.

1059
00:54:06,452 --> 00:54:08,819
I'm gonna need
a new team of scientists.

1060
00:54:08,913 --> 00:54:10,995
And I want them there
when we arrive.

1061
00:54:11,081 --> 00:54:12,412
Okay. DC?

1062
00:54:12,499 --> 00:54:14,911
Mm-mmm. No. The new place.

1063
00:54:15,002 --> 00:54:17,585
Oh. But, uh, we stopped
mid-renovation.

1064
00:54:17,671 --> 00:54:19,253
When we shut down the project.

1065
00:54:19,340 --> 00:54:22,503
Exactly.
We're officially unshut down.

1066
00:54:22,593 --> 00:54:25,005
What about Yelena
and the others?

1067
00:54:25,095 --> 00:54:26,130
Nothing yet.

1068
00:54:27,014 --> 00:54:28,880
Get rid of them, Mel.

1069
00:54:28,974 --> 00:54:30,806
They're the last piece
of evidence.

1070
00:54:31,393 --> 00:54:32,554
On it.

1071
00:54:32,645 --> 00:54:34,727
Let me know when our boy
in the box gets to New York.

1072
00:54:53,540 --> 00:54:56,248
[Ava, Walker, Yelena panting]

1073
00:54:57,503 --> 00:54:59,335
[Walker] Those birds
are way too high.

1074
00:54:59,421 --> 00:55:01,753
They're doing recon loops
at 4,000 feet.

1075
00:55:01,840 --> 00:55:03,626
I mean, they don't know
what they're doing.

1076
00:55:03,717 --> 00:55:05,799
They'll be five or ten klicks
away in no time.

1077
00:55:05,886 --> 00:55:08,253
All right, Walker, we get it.
You were in the military.

1078
00:55:08,347 --> 00:55:09,712
Five or ten klicks
to the bird.

1079
00:55:09,807 --> 00:55:10,797
[exclaims]

1080
00:55:15,479 --> 00:55:16,469
There.

1081
00:55:18,857 --> 00:55:22,521
[Walker] Uh, it's a...
I don't... What is that?

1082
00:55:22,611 --> 00:55:24,898
[car horn beeping]

1083
00:55:26,073 --> 00:55:28,189
Oh, no.

1084
00:55:28,909 --> 00:55:29,899
What?

1085
00:55:31,036 --> 00:55:32,367
[Walker]
It's coming right at us.

1086
00:55:32,454 --> 00:55:35,196
- [Ava] Who is that?
- It's no one.

1087
00:55:35,290 --> 00:55:36,371
It's nothing.

1088
00:55:36,458 --> 00:55:38,574
[beeping continues]

1089
00:55:44,258 --> 00:55:45,419
[beeping stops]

1090
00:55:45,509 --> 00:55:48,217
- Oh, God.
- Yelena!

1091
00:55:49,096 --> 00:55:51,463
It's your dad!

1092
00:55:51,557 --> 00:55:53,844
Don't go in the vault!

1093
00:55:53,934 --> 00:55:57,427
Valentina's gonna
burn you alive!

1094
00:56:00,065 --> 00:56:02,056
Yelena!

1095
00:56:03,819 --> 00:56:05,435
[Alexei] So, I finagled

1096
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:08,487
to pick up Miss de Fontaine
at fancy event.

1097
00:56:08,574 --> 00:56:10,656
I figure good networking,

1098
00:56:10,743 --> 00:56:13,656
but as soon as I overhear
the coordinates of the vault,

1099
00:56:13,746 --> 00:56:15,703
I rush home,
I get the tactical beast.

1100
00:56:15,789 --> 00:56:17,780
And then,
I drive straight here.

1101
00:56:17,875 --> 00:56:19,491
Oh, America's so big.

1102
00:56:19,585 --> 00:56:21,167
You ever drive
through Oklahoma?

1103
00:56:21,253 --> 00:56:22,243
It's so flat.

1104
00:56:22,337 --> 00:56:23,327
Oh, I forgot to tell you,

1105
00:56:23,422 --> 00:56:25,413
don't drink
from the Big Gulp back there.

1106
00:56:27,051 --> 00:56:28,382
[Yelena]
Alexei, have you slept?

1107
00:56:28,469 --> 00:56:30,255
I'll sleep when I'm dead!

1108
00:56:30,345 --> 00:56:32,473
Uh, I'd like not to die today.

1109
00:56:32,556 --> 00:56:34,172
So maybe somebody else
should be driving.

1110
00:56:34,266 --> 00:56:35,597
[Alexei] Mr. Walker,

1111
00:56:35,684 --> 00:56:38,176
second coming
of Captain America.

1112
00:56:38,270 --> 00:56:40,477
You and I have
lot in common, you know?

1113
00:56:40,564 --> 00:56:45,684
I too was state-sponsored
super soldier in Russia.

1114
00:56:45,778 --> 00:56:47,360
Mmm. But also very different

1115
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:49,653
because Walker actually knows
what he's doing.

1116
00:56:49,740 --> 00:56:52,903
[Alexei] And Ghost.
Ah, what a magician.

1117
00:56:52,993 --> 00:56:55,485
You disappear. You reappear.

1118
00:56:55,579 --> 00:56:57,195
When you reappear,
does sometimes things

1119
00:56:57,289 --> 00:56:58,905
not pop up in right place?

1120
00:56:58,999 --> 00:57:01,366
Oh. I find it best
just to ignore him sometimes.

1121
00:57:01,460 --> 00:57:03,497
What impressive friends
you've assembled, Yelena.

1122
00:57:03,587 --> 00:57:04,748
We are not friends, Alexei.

1123
00:57:04,838 --> 00:57:07,045
Nah. We're just
disposable delinquents.

1124
00:57:07,132 --> 00:57:08,418
Whatever you are,

1125
00:57:08,509 --> 00:57:10,625
the light inside you
is brighter, Yelena.

1126
00:57:12,513 --> 00:57:13,674
How about this?

1127
00:57:13,764 --> 00:57:17,632
You are a team
of scrappy antiheroes.

1128
00:57:17,726 --> 00:57:20,343
- Yeah. Go Thunderbolts.
- What?

1129
00:57:21,355 --> 00:57:22,595
- Yelena...
- Oh, my God.

1130
00:57:22,689 --> 00:57:24,350
You named them
after your peewee soccer club?

1131
00:57:24,441 --> 00:57:26,307
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God.
- [chuckles]

1132
00:57:26,401 --> 00:57:28,813
The West Chesapeake Valley
Thunderbolts.

1133
00:57:28,904 --> 00:57:30,065
Sponsored by

1134
00:57:30,155 --> 00:57:31,896
Dmitri's Elite Industrial
Lighting and Electronics.

1135
00:57:31,990 --> 00:57:32,980
No, no.

1136
00:57:33,075 --> 00:57:35,658
Never won a game,

1137
00:57:35,744 --> 00:57:37,530
but Yelena had so much fun.

1138
00:57:37,621 --> 00:57:38,907
There was a girl who pooped...

1139
00:57:38,997 --> 00:57:41,034
- No. It was-- It was not--
- ...In one game.

1140
00:57:41,125 --> 00:57:43,457
It was crazy.
I was yelling at the ref.

1141
00:57:43,544 --> 00:57:46,161
It was sponsored
by Shane's Tire Shop.

1142
00:57:46,255 --> 00:57:47,245
- Shane?
- Yes.

1143
00:57:47,339 --> 00:57:49,250
- What's this talk of Shane?
- It was.

1144
00:57:49,341 --> 00:57:50,706
He didn't have
that kind of money.

1145
00:57:50,801 --> 00:57:52,792
- Yes, it was.
- No! Shane? What a joke.

1146
00:57:52,886 --> 00:57:54,263
You really need to sleep.

1147
00:57:54,346 --> 00:57:56,758
Okay. What about
this Bob you mentioned?

1148
00:57:56,849 --> 00:57:58,510
What's the plan?
Where am I driving?

1149
00:57:58,600 --> 00:57:59,635
It's not like that.

1150
00:57:59,726 --> 00:58:01,717
We need to escape
and we need to hide.

1151
00:58:01,812 --> 00:58:03,268
Yeah, way smarter
for us to split up.

1152
00:58:03,355 --> 00:58:05,221
There's actually
an airfield not far from here.

1153
00:58:05,315 --> 00:58:06,430
We'll just disappear
from there.

1154
00:58:06,525 --> 00:58:08,812
Split up? No, no, no.

1155
00:58:08,902 --> 00:58:10,233
You may not see what I see,

1156
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:12,277
but I have been around
long time.

1157
00:58:12,364 --> 00:58:13,775
No shit.

1158
00:58:13,866 --> 00:58:17,200
This has the makings of a team
that can raise to glory.

1159
00:58:18,412 --> 00:58:21,871
A team that can bring light
from the darkness.

1160
00:58:21,957 --> 00:58:26,576
A team of heroes that can be
on the Wheaties box

1161
00:58:26,670 --> 00:58:30,288
- and have little kiddie toy...
- No, no.

1162
00:58:30,382 --> 00:58:33,249
This is not
a marketing opportunity, okay?

1163
00:58:33,343 --> 00:58:36,210
Valentina is hunting us,
and we cannot win.

1164
00:58:36,305 --> 00:58:37,295
Do you understand?

1165
00:58:37,389 --> 00:58:39,300
- You don't understand.
- I do. You don't.

1166
00:58:39,391 --> 00:58:41,849
Look, you say that Valentina
is going to use the power

1167
00:58:41,935 --> 00:58:43,050
- of this Sentry Project...
- Yes.

1168
00:58:43,145 --> 00:58:44,806
...to take over
and kill us all.

1169
00:58:44,897 --> 00:58:47,264
Then you need to
stand up to her.

1170
00:58:47,357 --> 00:58:49,348
You and your team.

1171
00:58:49,443 --> 00:58:51,480
You got a convoy
approaching fast.

1172
00:58:51,570 --> 00:58:53,732
- Step on it.
- Aye, aye, Captain.

1173
00:59:01,288 --> 00:59:02,403
[Ava] Is that it?

1174
00:59:02,497 --> 00:59:05,831
- Okay, any time now.
- Yeah. We're working on it.

1175
00:59:05,918 --> 00:59:07,500
- [Yelena] A little bit faster.
- [Alexei] Takes a second.

1176
00:59:07,586 --> 00:59:08,576
[Yelena] Alexei!

1177
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:15,583
- Alexei!
- Okay! Don't worry!

1178
00:59:15,677 --> 00:59:17,930
Don't worry.
She's bulletproof, huh?

1179
00:59:18,013 --> 00:59:20,550
Engaging defensive measures.

1180
00:59:20,641 --> 00:59:22,257
[♪ sensual R&B music playing,
Ginuwine "Pony"]

1181
00:59:22,351 --> 00:59:24,683
What the hell? [groaning]

1182
00:59:24,770 --> 00:59:26,306
Oh, my God.

1183
00:59:26,396 --> 00:59:28,057
Oh, shit. Wait, that's not
supposed to do that.

1184
00:59:28,148 --> 00:59:30,139
- [Yelena] Oh, my God.
- Come on.

1185
00:59:30,234 --> 00:59:31,520
Who are you driving?

1186
00:59:33,779 --> 00:59:35,110
Walker, shield!

1187
00:59:37,241 --> 00:59:38,948
What happened
to "bulletproof"?

1188
00:59:39,034 --> 00:59:40,695
- Bulletproof-ish.
- Jesus Christ!

1189
00:59:40,786 --> 00:59:42,777
God,
everyone's a critic today!

1190
00:59:44,623 --> 00:59:46,955
Time to break out
the bottle service.

1191
00:59:47,042 --> 00:59:48,953
Come on, Ghost,
give me the good stuff.

1192
00:59:49,795 --> 00:59:51,331
Okay, not really appropriate.

1193
00:59:51,421 --> 00:59:53,537
Vodka! Vodka, now!

1194
00:59:53,632 --> 00:59:56,294
Oh, my God.
This is so not the time.

1195
00:59:56,385 --> 00:59:58,843
[groans]
What's wrong with you?

1196
01:00:05,727 --> 01:00:07,513
[laughs]

1197
01:00:11,066 --> 01:00:12,682
No, no, no!

1198
01:00:16,405 --> 01:00:17,861
Give me a break.

1199
01:00:20,575 --> 01:00:23,567
[sighs]
Okay, I'll be back. I hope.

1200
01:00:27,541 --> 01:00:29,828
[high-pitched tone blares]

1201
01:00:34,047 --> 01:00:35,629
[grunts, groans]

1202
01:00:43,056 --> 01:00:45,468
[Alexei] Yelena!
What are you doing?

1203
01:00:45,559 --> 01:00:46,924
There's nothing you can do.

1204
01:00:53,984 --> 01:00:55,474
[Alexei] What?

1205
01:01:02,242 --> 01:01:04,153
[device beeping]

1206
01:01:16,465 --> 01:01:17,751
It's Bucky!

1207
01:01:18,925 --> 01:01:21,007
[chuckles] The Winter Soldier.

1208
01:01:33,899 --> 01:01:35,185
[engine revs]

1209
01:02:08,809 --> 01:02:11,892
[chuckles]
That's what I talk about!

1210
01:02:11,978 --> 01:02:13,935
- Yes! Yeah!
- Woo!

1211
01:02:19,736 --> 01:02:20,817
[cheering]

1212
01:02:20,904 --> 01:02:21,894
Oh, sh--

1213
01:02:31,706 --> 01:02:32,696
[reporter] Congressman!

1214
01:02:32,791 --> 01:02:34,327
Why did you call
an emergency session

1215
01:02:34,418 --> 01:02:35,624
of the impeachment committee?

1216
01:02:35,710 --> 01:02:36,791
What I can say

1217
01:02:36,878 --> 01:02:38,539
is that I've gotten
a tip from a trusted cohort

1218
01:02:38,630 --> 01:02:40,837
that will be
bringing some new evidence in,

1219
01:02:40,924 --> 01:02:42,289
and that evidence is juicy.

1220
01:02:42,384 --> 01:02:44,671
The impeachment
was just an appetizer.

1221
01:02:44,761 --> 01:02:46,672
They should be
getting a nice, cozy cell

1222
01:02:46,763 --> 01:02:49,380
in federal prison
ready for Miss Fontaine.

1223
01:02:50,142 --> 01:02:51,223
I just got word

1224
01:02:51,309 --> 01:02:52,845
the impeachment committee
is convening tonight.

1225
01:02:52,936 --> 01:02:53,971
This is serious, Val.

1226
01:02:54,062 --> 01:02:56,520
Were you able to
get the lab fully operational?

1227
01:02:56,606 --> 01:02:58,188
[Mel] Yes,
but the rest of the building

1228
01:02:58,275 --> 01:02:59,481
is only 70% finished.

1229
01:02:59,568 --> 01:03:01,730
[Valentina] Okay.
Mel, we'll get it there.

1230
01:03:01,820 --> 01:03:03,527
Welcome to the Watchtower.

1231
01:03:06,783 --> 01:03:07,773
[Mel] Val?

1232
01:03:07,868 --> 01:03:09,529
Something happened
in Malaysia.

1233
01:03:09,619 --> 01:03:10,700
Have you read his file?

1234
01:03:10,787 --> 01:03:12,778
Delusions of grandeur,
depression.

1235
01:03:12,873 --> 01:03:16,787
Someone that imbalanced
amplified by the treatment...

1236
01:03:16,877 --> 01:03:20,666
The people in the labs,
they were just test subjects.

1237
01:03:20,755 --> 01:03:22,291
They were never gonna
be the one.

1238
01:03:22,382 --> 01:03:24,419
Does this
look nurturing enough?

1239
01:03:26,511 --> 01:03:28,172
[sighs] Very nurturing.

1240
01:03:33,018 --> 01:03:36,852
Hi. How--
How are you feeling, Robert?

1241
01:03:36,938 --> 01:03:38,440
Are you comfortable?

1242
01:03:39,816 --> 01:03:40,806
Yeah.

1243
01:03:40,901 --> 01:03:45,566
My name is
Valentina Allegra de Fontaine.

1244
01:03:45,655 --> 01:03:47,908
Oh, no, no, no.
You-- You tried to kill us,

1245
01:03:47,991 --> 01:03:49,823
- didn't you?
- [shushes]

1246
01:03:53,955 --> 01:03:56,367
Let me explain.
Would-- Would you like that?

1247
01:03:57,876 --> 01:03:58,866
Yeah.

1248
01:03:58,960 --> 01:04:01,952
You signed up
for a medical study which was,

1249
01:04:02,047 --> 01:04:03,583
as advertised,

1250
01:04:03,673 --> 01:04:06,085
at the cutting edge
of human improvement.

1251
01:04:06,176 --> 01:04:08,338
But not everybody could handle

1252
01:04:08,428 --> 01:04:10,419
the amount of greatness
that we had in mind.

1253
01:04:10,514 --> 01:04:12,425
What happened to Yelena?

1254
01:04:12,516 --> 01:04:14,883
Yelena? Oh.

1255
01:04:14,976 --> 01:04:16,432
Well, those people
you were with,

1256
01:04:16,520 --> 01:04:17,885
those are not honest people.

1257
01:04:17,979 --> 01:04:20,721
They're criminals.
Villains, really.

1258
01:04:20,815 --> 01:04:23,477
No, no. They-- They helped me.

1259
01:04:24,236 --> 01:04:25,397
[Valentina scoffs]

1260
01:04:25,946 --> 01:04:27,528
Robert.

1261
01:04:27,614 --> 01:04:30,072
Let's just forget about them,
and let's focus on you.

1262
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:32,403
And how perfect you are.

1263
01:04:35,038 --> 01:04:36,028
Perfect, huh?

1264
01:04:36,122 --> 01:04:38,204
You always thought of yourself
as a victim.

1265
01:04:39,251 --> 01:04:40,833
But you overcame.

1266
01:04:40,919 --> 01:04:42,705
You went to Malaysia.

1267
01:04:42,796 --> 01:04:45,003
You were lost, right?
You were searching.

1268
01:04:46,550 --> 01:04:48,006
And you found me.

1269
01:04:48,093 --> 01:04:50,960
How--
How do you know all that?

1270
01:04:51,054 --> 01:04:52,089
I know all of it.

1271
01:04:52,180 --> 01:04:54,558
I know about
your mom's mental illness.

1272
01:04:54,641 --> 01:04:57,975
I know about your addiction
and your juvenile record.

1273
01:04:58,061 --> 01:05:00,723
I mean, I even know
about the times your father--

1274
01:05:00,814 --> 01:05:02,145
Stop! No, no, no.

1275
01:05:02,232 --> 01:05:03,643
I didn't say
you could know that.

1276
01:05:06,653 --> 01:05:09,611
[Valentina] Robert,
I know everything about you.

1277
01:05:09,698 --> 01:05:12,030
And I still want you
to be my guy.

1278
01:05:14,286 --> 01:05:15,868
And isn't that what you want?

1279
01:05:15,954 --> 01:05:18,821
To be accepted? To be chosen?

1280
01:05:20,041 --> 01:05:22,453
No one else sees it,

1281
01:05:22,544 --> 01:05:24,205
but I do.

1282
01:05:24,296 --> 01:05:28,585
And I think maybe your past
is what makes you so perfect.

1283
01:05:37,392 --> 01:05:39,099
[in Italian]
Stay quiet, Valentina.

1284
01:05:39,185 --> 01:05:41,847
Completely quiet,
no matter what you hear.

1285
01:05:41,938 --> 01:05:43,269
You promise me?

1286
01:05:43,356 --> 01:05:44,767
[Young Valentina]
Did I do something wrong?

1287
01:05:44,858 --> 01:05:47,600
The man in town
asked where we live.

1288
01:05:47,694 --> 01:05:50,436
He said he was your friend,
so I told him.

1289
01:05:50,530 --> 01:05:51,941
Yes, well he was.

1290
01:05:52,032 --> 01:05:54,945
Remember I told you
not to talk to anyone?

1291
01:05:55,035 --> 01:05:57,697
Yes, daddy. I'm so sorry.

1292
01:05:57,787 --> 01:06:00,495
It's okay.
Just stay hidden for me.

1293
01:06:00,582 --> 01:06:01,572
[banging on door]

1294
01:06:07,339 --> 01:06:08,420
You know...

1295
01:06:08,506 --> 01:06:10,634
I've been in this business
a long time.

1296
01:06:11,843 --> 01:06:14,961
There's always someone
like you, smart, but cocky.

1297
01:06:15,055 --> 01:06:17,387
A hungry dog who already had
a bone in his mouth.

1298
01:06:17,474 --> 01:06:19,590
[Valentina's dad]
Let's have a drink, shall we?

1299
01:06:20,310 --> 01:06:22,677
[man] You still think
you're getting away with this.

1300
01:06:23,855 --> 01:06:26,142
Don't worry, I'll look out
for your sweet Valentina.

1301
01:06:26,232 --> 01:06:27,222
[gunshot]

1302
01:06:35,533 --> 01:06:37,444
Would you excuse me
just for a moment?

1303
01:06:44,417 --> 01:06:46,408
No. All right.
Wait. Wait. Wait.

1304
01:06:50,465 --> 01:06:51,626
I can control it.

1305
01:06:56,805 --> 01:06:57,840
Great.

1306
01:07:03,311 --> 01:07:04,301
[Valentina] <i>All right.</i>

1307
01:07:04,396 --> 01:07:06,637
Let's get the press here
in the morning.

1308
01:07:06,731 --> 01:07:08,642
It's time to show everyone
what I've been working on.

1309
01:07:08,733 --> 01:07:12,192
Val, you put a serum into
someone like Steve Rogers,

1310
01:07:12,278 --> 01:07:13,609
he becomes Captain America,

1311
01:07:13,697 --> 01:07:16,815
but you do it
to someone this unstable,

1312
01:07:16,908 --> 01:07:18,615
I mean, who knows
what it did to him?

1313
01:07:18,702 --> 01:07:20,488
That's why
we build in safeguards.

1314
01:07:20,578 --> 01:07:21,784
Didn't we make a kill switch?

1315
01:07:21,871 --> 01:07:25,614
Yeah, but we threw it out
along with everything else.

1316
01:07:25,709 --> 01:07:27,620
Well, then remake it.

1317
01:07:27,711 --> 01:07:30,794
I don't really care
who this guy was.

1318
01:07:30,880 --> 01:07:33,133
I do know what he can become.

1319
01:07:34,634 --> 01:07:36,841
Get the press here
like I asked.

1320
01:07:46,563 --> 01:07:48,850
[Alexei] No, no, no, no!

1321
01:07:48,940 --> 01:07:51,898
Just when I get
my team together.

1322
01:07:51,985 --> 01:07:55,853
Mr. Soldier, you are making
terrible mistake.

1323
01:07:55,947 --> 01:07:57,779
Save it for the committee.

1324
01:07:57,866 --> 01:07:59,027
What committee?

1325
01:07:59,117 --> 01:08:00,107
You're all evidence

1326
01:08:00,201 --> 01:08:01,737
in the impeachment trial
against Valentina.

1327
01:08:01,828 --> 01:08:03,034
- [Walker laughs]
- [Ava laughs]

1328
01:08:03,121 --> 01:08:04,782
We don't even work
for Valentina anymore.

1329
01:08:04,873 --> 01:08:06,238
She tried to kill us.

1330
01:08:06,332 --> 01:08:07,618
We were ordered to destroy
all of her secrets,

1331
01:08:07,709 --> 01:08:09,575
but really, we were just sent
to kill each other

1332
01:08:09,669 --> 01:08:10,534
in this vault.

1333
01:08:10,628 --> 01:08:12,289
- But then we met Bob.
- Yeah. Bob.

1334
01:08:12,380 --> 01:08:14,462
[Yelena]
There was a man in the vault.

1335
01:08:14,549 --> 01:08:15,789
She's done something to him.

1336
01:08:15,884 --> 01:08:17,500
It's called Project Sentry.

1337
01:08:17,594 --> 01:08:20,336
Okay, he shot up into the sky.
He exploded.

1338
01:08:20,430 --> 01:08:21,886
And then he crashed
into this mountain,

1339
01:08:21,973 --> 01:08:23,134
and then he died, didn't die--

1340
01:08:23,224 --> 01:08:25,511
Yes, I got it.
He's very, very scary.

1341
01:08:25,602 --> 01:08:27,013
- So rude.
- Okay.

1342
01:08:27,103 --> 01:08:28,810
"Congressman Barnes."

1343
01:08:30,857 --> 01:08:31,847
All right, Walker.

1344
01:08:33,109 --> 01:08:34,395
What's that supposed to mean?

1345
01:08:34,486 --> 01:08:36,068
[Walker]
Means you know me, Bucky.

1346
01:08:36,154 --> 01:08:38,691
So cut the shit and listen to
what we're trying to tell you.

1347
01:08:38,782 --> 01:08:39,988
[Bucky]
Yeah, I know you, John,

1348
01:08:40,074 --> 01:08:42,532
and you made your choices.

1349
01:08:42,619 --> 01:08:43,609
I know it's been hard

1350
01:08:43,703 --> 01:08:45,159
since Olivia left you
and took your kid,

1351
01:08:45,246 --> 01:08:47,283
but still, this is on you.

1352
01:08:50,877 --> 01:08:53,790
[Ava] Bucky, there won't be
a committee left. Okay?

1353
01:08:53,880 --> 01:08:55,416
There might not
even be a government.

1354
01:08:55,507 --> 01:08:56,838
She has some big--

1355
01:08:56,925 --> 01:08:58,836
[Bucky] Threat. Yes. I got it.

1356
01:08:58,927 --> 01:09:01,885
Named "Bob" or "Sentry”
who flies. Right?

1357
01:09:01,971 --> 01:09:02,881
And you're all heroes

1358
01:09:02,972 --> 01:09:04,554
going after Val,
ready to save the day.

1359
01:09:04,641 --> 01:09:05,756
Am I supposed to believe that?

1360
01:09:05,850 --> 01:09:07,136
We weren't going
after her together.

1361
01:09:07,227 --> 01:09:09,184
We were just trying
to get home alive, actually.

1362
01:09:09,270 --> 01:09:10,522
[Bucky]
That's even more pathetic.

1363
01:09:10,605 --> 01:09:12,346
Yeah, I know. That's what
I've been telling them.

1364
01:09:12,440 --> 01:09:14,056
- Shut up.
- I'm not going to shut up. No.

1365
01:09:14,150 --> 01:09:15,811
All right.
Plane lands in six minutes.

1366
01:09:15,902 --> 01:09:17,438
- [Yelena] Will you be quiet?
- Yes?

1367
01:09:17,529 --> 01:09:18,985
Bucky, I need your help.

1368
01:09:19,572 --> 01:09:20,824
What is it?

1369
01:09:20,907 --> 01:09:23,114
Val has gone off the rails.

1370
01:09:23,201 --> 01:09:25,112
I mean, Project Sentry,
it's not just a failure,

1371
01:09:25,203 --> 01:09:26,409
<i>it's dangerous.</i>

1372
01:09:26,496 --> 01:09:27,452
Project Sentry?

1373
01:09:27,539 --> 01:09:29,701
[shushes]

1374
01:09:29,791 --> 01:09:31,577
[Mel] <i>She has too much power
in her hands.</i>

1375
01:09:31,668 --> 01:09:34,786
<i>And this guy is a disaster
waiting to happen.</i>

1376
01:09:34,879 --> 01:09:37,086
- What guy?
- [sighs] Bob.

1377
01:09:37,173 --> 01:09:38,163
Bob?

1378
01:09:38,758 --> 01:09:40,089
Bob!

1379
01:09:40,176 --> 01:09:41,462
[Mel] <i>We're at
the old Avengers place.</i>

1380
01:09:41,553 --> 01:09:43,715
<i>The press are set to come
tomorrow morning.</i>

1381
01:09:43,805 --> 01:09:45,762
Someone has to do something.

1382
01:09:45,849 --> 01:09:48,557
Shit. Okay, I-- I have to go.
But come now, please.

1383
01:09:48,643 --> 01:09:50,509
<i>Bring anyone.
Everyone you can.</i>

1384
01:09:50,603 --> 01:09:52,059
[line disconnects]

1385
01:09:59,362 --> 01:10:00,193
Bob.

1386
01:10:00,280 --> 01:10:02,362
- Bob.
- How many times?

1387
01:10:02,448 --> 01:10:03,438
I Know.

1388
01:10:04,617 --> 01:10:06,153
It's bad, Bucky.

1389
01:10:16,045 --> 01:10:18,207
[Ava] Hang on.
What are you doing?

1390
01:10:18,298 --> 01:10:20,414
I'm letting you go.
You're coming with me.

1391
01:10:20,508 --> 01:10:21,498
Why?

1392
01:10:21,593 --> 01:10:23,175
[shushes]

1393
01:10:23,261 --> 01:10:25,127
For the glory.

1394
01:10:25,221 --> 01:10:26,928
Well, you know Valentina.

1395
01:10:27,015 --> 01:10:29,222
She's got this thing
out there.

1396
01:10:29,309 --> 01:10:31,767
People are gonna get hurt,
and I gotta stop her.

1397
01:10:31,853 --> 01:10:33,264
And you are gonna help me.

1398
01:10:33,354 --> 01:10:34,890
Wait. Us?

1399
01:10:34,981 --> 01:10:36,847
Why? You got some place to be?

1400
01:10:38,568 --> 01:10:40,479
Bucky, you have
the wrong people.

1401
01:10:41,029 --> 01:10:42,269
[sighs]

1402
01:10:44,240 --> 01:10:46,231
Look, I've been where you are.

1403
01:10:47,827 --> 01:10:49,613
You can run,
but it doesn't go away.

1404
01:10:50,663 --> 01:10:52,074
Sooner or later
it catches up to you,

1405
01:10:52,165 --> 01:10:53,872
and when it does,
it's too late.

1406
01:10:56,461 --> 01:10:58,668
So you can either
do something about it now,

1407
01:11:00,173 --> 01:11:01,584
or live with it forever.

1408
01:11:10,224 --> 01:11:11,555
[Yelena sighs]

1409
01:11:12,435 --> 01:11:14,301
Stop Val and save Bob.

1410
01:11:16,439 --> 01:11:17,554
- Fine.
- Mmm?

1411
01:11:17,649 --> 01:11:18,764
Yeah.

1412
01:11:21,986 --> 01:11:22,976
Go on, then.

1413
01:11:24,906 --> 01:11:27,898
Yes!

1414
01:11:27,992 --> 01:11:29,198
Yeah!

1415
01:11:34,707 --> 01:11:36,789
What'd you think
this job was gonna be?

1416
01:11:38,711 --> 01:11:39,701
[chuckles]

1417
01:11:39,796 --> 01:11:42,754
I don't know.
I hope I've done some good.

1418
01:11:42,840 --> 01:11:44,092
"Good."

1419
01:11:45,218 --> 01:11:47,255
Good girl. Good enough.

1420
01:11:47,345 --> 01:11:48,801
[scoffs]

1421
01:11:48,888 --> 01:11:50,595
You want to be good?

1422
01:11:50,682 --> 01:11:53,299
Or do you want to be somebody
who changes the world?

1423
01:11:53,977 --> 01:11:55,559
Can't I be both?

1424
01:11:55,645 --> 01:11:57,807
I mean, I thought you wanted
to change the world

1425
01:11:57,897 --> 01:11:59,058
for the better too.

1426
01:11:59,148 --> 01:12:04,018
Mel, righteousness without
power is just an opinion.

1427
01:12:04,112 --> 01:12:07,104
Look, you're brought up
to believe

1428
01:12:07,198 --> 01:12:09,280
that there's a good guy
and a bad guy.

1429
01:12:09,367 --> 01:12:12,029
But then eventually,
you come to realize

1430
01:12:13,037 --> 01:12:16,496
that there's a bad guy
and a worse guy.

1431
01:12:17,291 --> 01:12:18,793
And nothing else.

1432
01:12:19,460 --> 01:12:21,371
Let me know when
you come to your senses.

1433
01:12:25,049 --> 01:12:27,791
[deep breathing]

1434
01:12:27,885 --> 01:12:28,920
[groans]

1435
01:12:29,012 --> 01:12:30,423
Um, I don't know. [chuckles]

1436
01:12:30,513 --> 01:12:32,049
Okay, yeah. We just try again.

1437
01:12:32,140 --> 01:12:32,971
Yeah.

1438
01:12:33,057 --> 01:12:34,843
Let's just focus.

1439
01:12:34,934 --> 01:12:36,049
Mmm.

1440
01:12:37,270 --> 01:12:38,260
I believe in you.

1441
01:13:01,794 --> 01:13:02,784
[exhales sharply]

1442
01:13:03,379 --> 01:13:04,540
I can do that?

1443
01:13:06,632 --> 01:13:08,134
You can do anything.

1444
01:13:09,469 --> 01:13:11,756
People think they know you.
[scoffs]

1445
01:13:12,513 --> 01:13:14,345
They just see you as "Bob."

1446
01:13:14,432 --> 01:13:15,672
They pity Bob.

1447
01:13:16,559 --> 01:13:18,550
I'm the only one who knows

1448
01:13:18,644 --> 01:13:20,976
what your true potential is,
Robert.

1449
01:13:22,648 --> 01:13:23,934
And it's limitless.

1450
01:13:24,025 --> 01:13:25,015
[chuckles]

1451
01:13:26,986 --> 01:13:28,272
Ready for the next lesson?

1452
01:13:40,458 --> 01:13:42,574
And then I have
these little, Widow...

1453
01:13:42,668 --> 01:13:44,329
[imitates buzzing]
...bite things.

1454
01:13:44,420 --> 01:13:45,922
- And in the left...
- Yeah. I-- I remember.

1455
01:13:46,005 --> 01:13:48,167
And then I have this 19.

1456
01:13:49,258 --> 01:13:51,590
Forty-five. The long barrel.

1457
01:13:51,677 --> 01:13:52,587
[Ava] Mmm.

1458
01:13:52,678 --> 01:13:54,544
- Wow. It's big.
- Yeah. Well, it's--

1459
01:13:54,639 --> 01:13:55,754
- It's long.
- [Ava] Mmm.

1460
01:13:55,848 --> 01:13:56,929
- Yeah.
- [Ava] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1461
01:13:57,016 --> 01:13:59,178
- Okay, it's a little long.
- [Ava] Yeah. Big gun.

1462
01:13:59,268 --> 01:14:01,646
And, uh... your--
what about your hat?

1463
01:14:01,729 --> 01:14:04,471
Uh, the hat? The-- The helmet?

1464
01:14:04,565 --> 01:14:06,476
Yeah. Whatever you want
to call it.

1465
01:14:06,567 --> 01:14:08,604
It's, like, cool. Right?
You like it?

1466
01:14:08,694 --> 01:14:10,480
Do-- Do you like the hat?

1467
01:14:12,698 --> 01:14:14,860
Yeah, I think
the hat's pretty--

1468
01:14:14,951 --> 01:14:16,066
- Pretty sweet.
- Then, cool.

1469
01:14:16,160 --> 01:14:18,276
What kind of super serum
did you get?

1470
01:14:19,872 --> 01:14:21,829
I don't know. Regular. Hydra.

1471
01:14:21,916 --> 01:14:22,951
Hydra? Oh.

1472
01:14:23,042 --> 01:14:24,282
- Fancy.
- Yes.

1473
01:14:24,377 --> 01:14:27,460
Mine was Soviet recreation.
But it's still good, you know?

1474
01:14:27,964 --> 01:14:28,954
[chuckles]

1475
01:14:29,048 --> 01:14:31,210
- We are same. You and me.
- Well...

1476
01:14:31,300 --> 01:14:33,712
I mean, we are different,
but we are same.

1477
01:14:33,803 --> 01:14:35,544
You know, we could
be coleaders in this, huh?

1478
01:14:35,638 --> 01:14:36,628
[Bucky] Little different.

1479
01:14:36,722 --> 01:14:39,134
You get tired, I drive.

1480
01:14:39,225 --> 01:14:40,465
Huh? [chuckles]

1481
01:14:40,560 --> 01:14:41,550
I don't get tired.

1482
01:14:41,644 --> 01:14:42,930
No, I mean metaphorically.

1483
01:14:43,020 --> 01:14:44,272
I don't actually
want to drive.

1484
01:14:44,355 --> 01:14:45,720
[Yelena] Are we there yet?

1485
01:14:45,815 --> 01:14:47,397
- Almost!
- Almost!

1486
01:14:47,483 --> 01:14:48,814
[breathes deeply]

1487
01:14:48,901 --> 01:14:54,146
Okay. Mr. Soldier,
what is secret plan, huh?

1488
01:14:55,116 --> 01:14:56,106
The plan?

1489
01:14:56,617 --> 01:14:57,607
Yeah.

1490
01:14:59,162 --> 01:15:00,152
[wheels screech]

1491
01:15:05,126 --> 01:15:06,457
[guard] Open up on him!

1492
01:15:06,961 --> 01:15:08,872
- [guard] Go, go!
- [guard 2] Open up!

1493
01:15:09,589 --> 01:15:11,205
- [guards yelling]
- I like this plan.

1494
01:15:17,555 --> 01:15:18,670
[shouts]

1495
01:15:21,309 --> 01:15:22,720
[both grunting]

1496
01:15:42,038 --> 01:15:43,119
[alarm blares]

1497
01:15:43,206 --> 01:15:44,571
[Valentina on PA]
<i>Jesus, you guys,</i>

1498
01:15:44,665 --> 01:15:46,326
<i>I literally just
put that drywall in.</i>

1499
01:15:46,417 --> 01:15:48,909
<i>I left the door unlocked
for you.</i>

1500
01:15:49,003 --> 01:15:50,038
<i>Come up.</i>

1501
01:15:50,796 --> 01:15:52,503
[guard gasps, groans]

1502
01:15:55,009 --> 01:15:55,999
[grunts]

1503
01:15:59,388 --> 01:16:00,503
[elevator bell dings]

1504
01:16:06,979 --> 01:16:10,597
How crazy is it to think
of all the monumental fights

1505
01:16:10,691 --> 01:16:13,649
that happened exactly here
where you're standing?

1506
01:16:14,904 --> 01:16:17,271
Eh. I don't really care.

1507
01:16:17,365 --> 01:16:19,276
I mean, the place
wasn't cheap,

1508
01:16:19,367 --> 01:16:21,324
but it's got good optics.

1509
01:16:21,410 --> 01:16:22,992
[Bucky]
Well, it's over, Valentina.

1510
01:16:23,079 --> 01:16:24,490
This ends today.

1511
01:16:24,580 --> 01:16:26,617
Congressman Barnes, wow.

1512
01:16:26,707 --> 01:16:27,993
You know,
I never really thought

1513
01:16:28,084 --> 01:16:30,542
you'd have
a promising political career.

1514
01:16:30,628 --> 01:16:32,790
But less than half a term?

1515
01:16:33,631 --> 01:16:34,621
Yikes.

1516
01:16:35,716 --> 01:16:36,922
We're taking you in, Val.

1517
01:16:37,468 --> 01:16:38,583
[scoffs]

1518
01:16:38,678 --> 01:16:40,043
I don't think so.

1519
01:16:40,137 --> 01:16:42,845
[chuckling] Junior Varsity
Captain America.

1520
01:16:44,016 --> 01:16:45,131
[Bucky] Walker.

1521
01:16:46,644 --> 01:16:48,681
Oh, nice to see you, Ava.

1522
01:16:50,064 --> 01:16:53,056
Yelena. You look awful.

1523
01:16:54,026 --> 01:16:55,482
You sure you're really ready

1524
01:16:55,569 --> 01:16:57,560
for that public facing role
you asked me about?

1525
01:16:57,655 --> 01:17:00,488
Eat shit, Valentina.
Where's Bob?

1526
01:17:00,574 --> 01:17:03,987
Look at you.
You are all so adorable.

1527
01:17:04,078 --> 01:17:07,196
Just think, I send you
down there to Kill each other,

1528
01:17:07,290 --> 01:17:10,658
and instead, you make nice
and you form a team.

1529
01:17:11,919 --> 01:17:13,250
Who's this old Santa?

1530
01:17:14,714 --> 01:17:16,045
I'm Alexei Shostakov.

1531
01:17:17,925 --> 01:17:19,256
The Red Guardian.

1532
01:17:20,553 --> 01:17:21,509
What?

1533
01:17:23,347 --> 01:17:24,724
- Where's Mel?
- Mel?

1534
01:17:24,807 --> 01:17:26,047
Oh, Mel. Yeah.

1535
01:17:26,142 --> 01:17:29,385
Uh, Mel is having
a little loyalty issue.

1536
01:17:29,478 --> 01:17:32,015
But I'm just so grateful

1537
01:17:32,106 --> 01:17:35,394
that she stayed long enough
to lure you all in.

1538
01:17:39,530 --> 01:17:40,816
I'm not alone.

1539
01:17:42,158 --> 01:17:43,148
Robert?

1540
01:17:47,580 --> 01:17:48,570
Oh, my God.

1541
01:17:50,791 --> 01:17:51,781
[Bucky] That's Bob?

1542
01:17:51,876 --> 01:17:54,038
Yeah, he's changed a little.

1543
01:17:56,339 --> 01:17:59,502
It is my great honor

1544
01:17:59,592 --> 01:18:02,175
to introduce to you
The Sentry.

1545
01:18:04,096 --> 01:18:05,427
Hey, guys.

1546
01:18:05,514 --> 01:18:07,926
Wow. That's cool name.

1547
01:18:08,017 --> 01:18:10,850
[Valentina]
All-powerful. Invincible.

1548
01:18:10,936 --> 01:18:14,065
Stronger than all of
the Avengers rolled into one.

1549
01:18:14,148 --> 01:18:18,893
And soon to be known
as Earth's mightiest hero.

1550
01:18:20,529 --> 01:18:22,145
Have you dyed your hair?

1551
01:18:22,239 --> 01:18:23,855
Yeah. Well, it was...

1552
01:18:23,949 --> 01:18:24,984
Yeah, it was my idea.

1553
01:18:26,035 --> 01:18:28,572
People love a classic hero.

1554
01:18:28,662 --> 01:18:31,199
Okay, I'll bite.
What's the plan?

1555
01:18:31,290 --> 01:18:33,122
You haven't
figured it out yet, Bucky?

1556
01:18:33,209 --> 01:18:34,199
Geez.

1557
01:18:34,293 --> 01:18:35,829
Well, at least
you're kind of cute.

1558
01:18:35,920 --> 01:18:37,752
You're not
going to hurt people.

1559
01:18:38,506 --> 01:18:39,541
Oh, no.

1560
01:18:39,632 --> 01:18:41,714
No, I'm not gonna hurt people.

1561
01:18:41,801 --> 01:18:43,087
I'm gonna hurt you.

1562
01:18:43,177 --> 01:18:46,715
You see, the press is
on their way here now.

1563
01:18:46,806 --> 01:18:49,673
And they're gonna witness
the awesome power of Sentry

1564
01:18:49,767 --> 01:18:54,011
as he takes down this ruthless
group of rogue agents,

1565
01:18:54,105 --> 01:18:56,142
thus beginning a new era

1566
01:18:56,232 --> 01:19:00,191
in which I decide how to keep
the American people safe,

1567
01:19:00,277 --> 01:19:01,779
answering to no one.

1568
01:19:03,239 --> 01:19:05,355
I'll be unimpeachable.

1569
01:19:05,449 --> 01:19:08,316
That's... never gonna happen.

1570
01:19:09,662 --> 01:19:14,623
Sentry, your first mission is
to take out these criminals.

1571
01:19:19,088 --> 01:19:21,705
I don't wanna hurt you guys.

1572
01:19:21,799 --> 01:19:24,632
Why don't you just turn
yourselves in? [chuckles]

1573
01:19:24,718 --> 01:19:27,050
No, you don't
wanna do this, Bobby.

1574
01:19:28,222 --> 01:19:30,008
You can call me The Sentry.

1575
01:19:30,099 --> 01:19:31,214
Please, don't do this.

1576
01:19:31,308 --> 01:19:33,049
You do not need
to listen to her.

1577
01:19:33,144 --> 01:19:35,431
Robert, they don't think
you're good enough.

1578
01:19:35,521 --> 01:19:37,728
- That's not true.
- [Valentina] Remember?

1579
01:19:37,815 --> 01:19:39,931
You can trust me. I know you.

1580
01:19:42,027 --> 01:19:43,358
I don't think that you do.

1581
01:19:47,116 --> 01:19:48,698
Enough talking!

1582
01:19:49,368 --> 01:19:50,824
No one messes

1583
01:19:50,911 --> 01:19:55,496
with the West Chesapeake
Valley Thunderbolts!

1584
01:19:55,583 --> 01:19:57,244
- [Alexei shouts]
- Thunderbolts?

1585
01:20:00,337 --> 01:20:02,169
Hey. No, no, no! No!

1586
01:20:06,135 --> 01:20:07,250
Wait!

1587
01:20:07,344 --> 01:20:08,470
Bob, no!

1588
01:20:15,853 --> 01:20:16,809
[Yelena] Alexei, wait!

1589
01:20:27,364 --> 01:20:28,775
[screaming]

1590
01:20:53,140 --> 01:20:54,301
Stop, Bob.

1591
01:21:14,078 --> 01:21:16,410
[all groaning]

1592
01:21:58,706 --> 01:22:01,164
[Valentina] I'm so glad you
were able to catch a glimpse

1593
01:22:01,250 --> 01:22:02,411
before your, uh...

1594
01:22:03,127 --> 01:22:04,333
retirement. [chuckles]

1595
01:22:06,422 --> 01:22:09,039
Camera crews are assembling.

1596
01:22:09,133 --> 01:22:10,464
Finish the job, Robert.

1597
01:22:11,927 --> 01:22:13,167
[Sentry] Finish the job?

1598
01:22:15,055 --> 01:22:16,045
No.

1599
01:22:17,433 --> 01:22:18,719
What?

1600
01:22:18,809 --> 01:22:22,894
They're not a threat to me,
so why do I need to kill them?

1601
01:22:24,815 --> 01:22:27,056
You need to do
what I say, Robert.

1602
01:22:30,362 --> 01:22:31,352
Why?

1603
01:22:32,906 --> 01:22:33,896
"Why"?

1604
01:22:38,537 --> 01:22:41,655
[Alexei]
Okay. We need new plan.

1605
01:22:41,749 --> 01:22:44,491
[Walker] Nah, no new plans.

1606
01:22:44,585 --> 01:22:47,577
That thing is just
too powerful.

1607
01:22:47,671 --> 01:22:50,049
We just need to regroup
and think.

1608
01:22:50,132 --> 01:22:51,668
There's got to be a way
to stop that guy.

1609
01:22:51,759 --> 01:22:53,341
[Walker] Oh, my God.
We're not regrouping.

1610
01:22:53,427 --> 01:22:55,464
- This isn't even a team.
- Of course we're a team.

1611
01:22:55,554 --> 01:22:57,170
We are the Thunderbolts.

1612
01:22:57,264 --> 01:22:58,641
I don't know what that means.

1613
01:22:58,724 --> 01:23:00,681
It's her peewee
soccer team thing. It's--

1614
01:23:00,768 --> 01:23:02,258
We need to go somewhere
to discuss this.

1615
01:23:02,353 --> 01:23:04,310
- Discuss what?
- We are going to regroup.

1616
01:23:04,396 --> 01:23:05,431
We are going to go
back in there.

1617
01:23:05,522 --> 01:23:06,683
He turned my shield
into a taco.

1618
01:23:06,774 --> 01:23:08,390
Oh, my God! Stop.

1619
01:23:10,402 --> 01:23:13,736
There is no "us."
There is no "we."

1620
01:23:13,822 --> 01:23:15,779
Bob changed into that thing,

1621
01:23:15,866 --> 01:23:18,107
and there's nothing
any of you can do about it.

1622
01:23:18,202 --> 01:23:19,909
And what did you do exactly?

1623
01:23:19,995 --> 01:23:21,827
'Cause I seem to remember
you getting your arse beat

1624
01:23:21,914 --> 01:23:22,779
way worse than mine.

1625
01:23:22,873 --> 01:23:25,865
Yeah. Yeah.
I suck. I'm terrible.

1626
01:23:25,959 --> 01:23:27,916
We're all terrible.

1627
01:23:28,003 --> 01:23:30,620
Ava, you're not a hero.
You're not even a good person.

1628
01:23:31,382 --> 01:23:32,213
Bitch.

1629
01:23:32,299 --> 01:23:33,585
[scoffs] See?

1630
01:23:33,676 --> 01:23:34,666
Slow down. <i>Um-nichka.</i>

1631
01:23:34,760 --> 01:23:36,797
Alexei, I am not
your <i>um-nichka.</i>

1632
01:23:36,887 --> 01:23:39,470
I haven't heard from you
or seen you in a year.

1633
01:23:39,556 --> 01:23:41,092
[Walker] Okay, go easy on him.

1634
01:23:41,183 --> 01:23:43,265
- Oh, so you're nice now?
- Is it my turn?

1635
01:23:43,352 --> 01:23:45,138
No, you know you're
a piece of trash, Walker.

1636
01:23:45,229 --> 01:23:46,219
So does your family.

1637
01:23:46,313 --> 01:23:47,519
Jesus.

1638
01:23:48,941 --> 01:23:50,272
We're all losers.

1639
01:23:52,027 --> 01:23:53,483
And we lost. [scoffs]

1640
01:24:00,703 --> 01:24:01,693
Yelena!

1641
01:24:03,789 --> 01:24:06,247
It-- It needs to be
more of a collaboration.

1642
01:24:06,333 --> 01:24:07,949
The hair, for example.

1643
01:24:08,043 --> 01:24:10,080
Maybe-- Maybe I should have
had more of a say.

1644
01:24:10,170 --> 01:24:12,036
Don't let those idiots
get in your head.

1645
01:24:12,131 --> 01:24:13,917
The blond is great.

1646
01:24:14,007 --> 01:24:15,213
You sure?
'Cause, I don't know,

1647
01:24:15,300 --> 01:24:16,961
I thought I liked it.
Now I'm not so sure.

1648
01:24:17,052 --> 01:24:18,167
Enough about the hair.

1649
01:24:18,262 --> 01:24:19,468
Well, it's not just
about the hair.

1650
01:24:19,555 --> 01:24:21,216
Well, you keep talking
about the hair.

1651
01:24:21,306 --> 01:24:25,095
No, it's everything. My suit.
My name. My missions.

1652
01:24:25,185 --> 01:24:26,175
I mean...

1653
01:24:27,521 --> 01:24:28,807
why...

1654
01:24:28,897 --> 01:24:33,516
why would a god take orders
from anyone at all?

1655
01:24:33,610 --> 01:24:35,817
I think you're throwing around
the word "god"

1656
01:24:35,904 --> 01:24:37,156
a bit loosely there.

1657
01:24:37,239 --> 01:24:40,277
No, no. Because you said I was
all-powerful, invincible,

1658
01:24:40,367 --> 01:24:42,358
and stronger than
a whole team of Avengers,

1659
01:24:42,453 --> 01:24:45,036
which includes
at least one god, so...

1660
01:24:48,709 --> 01:24:49,790
But I'm starting to think

1661
01:24:49,877 --> 01:24:53,040
maybe you don't
know what I am.

1662
01:24:54,298 --> 01:24:56,164
Oh, goddamn it.

1663
01:24:56,258 --> 01:24:57,760
[Bob] Or what I'm capable of.

1664
01:24:59,970 --> 01:25:01,881
- [Valentina sighs]
- Maybe I need to show you.

1665
01:25:02,765 --> 01:25:06,053
[sighs] This is so irritating.

1666
01:25:13,066 --> 01:25:14,648
You were gonna turn on me,

1667
01:25:16,320 --> 01:25:17,776
just like the rest of them.

1668
01:25:18,739 --> 01:25:20,946
I'm not afraid of you, Robert.

1669
01:25:21,033 --> 01:25:22,569
[chuckles]

1670
01:25:22,659 --> 01:25:25,117
It's not Robert
you need to be afraid of.

1671
01:25:28,540 --> 01:25:29,530
[Valentina coughs]

1672
01:25:31,877 --> 01:25:32,958
[device clicks]

1673
01:25:35,881 --> 01:25:36,871
[sighs]

1674
01:25:40,385 --> 01:25:42,046
Good girl.

1675
01:25:42,137 --> 01:25:43,673
You came to your senses.

1676
01:25:45,933 --> 01:25:47,219
Come here. Help me up.

1677
01:25:50,395 --> 01:25:52,386
- I want a raise.
- Hmm.

1678
01:25:52,481 --> 01:25:53,767
- [elevator bell dings]
- [Valentina] Okay, fine.

1679
01:25:53,857 --> 01:25:55,143
Get cleanup on the body.

1680
01:25:55,234 --> 01:25:56,850
And tell Holt
it's finally time

1681
01:25:56,944 --> 01:25:58,434
to go lethal on these losers.

1682
01:26:15,254 --> 01:26:16,369
[Alexei] Yelena!

1683
01:26:17,840 --> 01:26:18,875
- Little one.
- Go away.

1684
01:26:18,966 --> 01:26:19,956
No, I will not.

1685
01:26:20,050 --> 01:26:21,916
Well, then, chase me forever.

1686
01:26:22,010 --> 01:26:24,126
Fine, I will, because
that's what family does.

1687
01:26:24,221 --> 01:26:25,928
Oh, my God, stop.

1688
01:26:26,014 --> 01:26:27,800
If you cared,
you would have called.

1689
01:26:27,891 --> 01:26:29,393
I would have heard from you.

1690
01:26:31,895 --> 01:26:35,183
I lost my sister again,
but forever.

1691
01:26:37,401 --> 01:26:38,732
And you disappeared.

1692
01:26:38,819 --> 01:26:40,105
[Alexei speaks Russian]

1693
01:26:40,195 --> 01:26:41,185
I'm sorry.

1694
01:26:43,198 --> 01:26:44,700
I don't know how to do this.

1695
01:26:46,785 --> 01:26:48,071
I'm not good at it.

1696
01:26:50,914 --> 01:26:52,621
I didn't think you wanted me.

1697
01:26:57,004 --> 01:26:58,085
I did.

1698
01:27:00,674 --> 01:27:01,755
I see that.

1699
01:27:04,011 --> 01:27:07,299
I'm late, but I'm...
I'm here now.

1700
01:27:11,602 --> 01:27:13,309
Daddy, I'm so alone.

1701
01:27:15,856 --> 01:27:17,847
I don't have anything anymore.

1702
01:27:20,235 --> 01:27:24,695
All I do is sit
and look at my phone

1703
01:27:24,781 --> 01:27:27,273
and think of all the terrible
things that I've done.

1704
01:27:27,367 --> 01:27:29,904
And then I go to work.
And then I drink.

1705
01:27:29,995 --> 01:27:31,952
And then I come home
to no one.

1706
01:27:32,039 --> 01:27:33,200
And I sit

1707
01:27:33,290 --> 01:27:34,872
and I think about all
the terrible things I've done

1708
01:27:34,958 --> 01:27:36,335
- again and again.
- Yelena, stop. Stop.

1709
01:27:36,418 --> 01:27:37,283
And I go crazy.

1710
01:27:37,377 --> 01:27:38,913
We all have things
that we regret.

1711
01:27:39,004 --> 01:27:40,494
No, but I have so many.

1712
01:27:43,050 --> 01:27:46,884
My first test at the Red Room.

1713
01:27:48,221 --> 01:27:50,053
Anya. She was just a child.

1714
01:27:50,140 --> 01:27:52,131
- She was so small.
- So were you.

1715
01:27:54,061 --> 01:27:55,267
I Know.

1716
01:27:55,354 --> 01:27:59,313
I know there were dark times.
Very, very dark times.

1717
01:27:59,399 --> 01:28:03,313
But before, you were such
a special little girl.

1718
01:28:03,403 --> 01:28:04,734
Did you know this?

1719
01:28:06,907 --> 01:28:09,899
You walked into a room.
You made it brighter.

1720
01:28:10,953 --> 01:28:13,115
You felt a lot of joy.

1721
01:28:14,206 --> 01:28:17,198
I don't remember that feeling.

1722
01:28:17,292 --> 01:28:18,748
You were so kind.

1723
01:28:20,879 --> 01:28:22,836
Do you remember why
you want to be goalie

1724
01:28:22,923 --> 01:28:24,755
on your terrible soccer team?

1725
01:28:26,134 --> 01:28:27,124
I...

1726
01:28:28,387 --> 01:28:30,173
So I didn't have
to run as much.

1727
01:28:30,263 --> 01:28:31,094
[chuckling] No.

1728
01:28:31,181 --> 01:28:33,718
Maybe that too,
but you told me,

1729
01:28:34,810 --> 01:28:38,053
"I want to be the one
everyone can rely on

1730
01:28:38,146 --> 01:28:40,228
if they make a mistake."

1731
01:28:41,483 --> 01:28:44,441
That Lena is still in you.

1732
01:28:45,696 --> 01:28:47,186
I still see her.

1733
01:28:49,408 --> 01:28:50,773
I don't.

1734
01:28:50,867 --> 01:28:54,076
You're stuck. You're alone.
You look only at the bad.

1735
01:28:54,162 --> 01:28:58,827
When I look at you,
I don't see your mistakes.

1736
01:29:01,253 --> 01:29:02,664
That's why we need each other.

1737
01:29:08,093 --> 01:29:09,583
Okay, that was really good.

1738
01:29:11,972 --> 01:29:13,963
[people chattering]

1739
01:29:26,278 --> 01:29:27,359
- Val?
- Yeah?

1740
01:29:27,446 --> 01:29:28,982
It's cleanup
from the penthouse,

1741
01:29:29,072 --> 01:29:31,689
and they're saying, well,
there's no body.

1742
01:29:32,617 --> 01:29:33,607
What?

1743
01:29:36,204 --> 01:29:37,194
[gasps]

1744
01:29:49,342 --> 01:29:51,470
[agent] <i>I don't know
what I'm looking at up here.</i>

1745
01:29:51,553 --> 01:29:53,135
<i>It doesn't look good.</i>

1746
01:30:00,312 --> 01:30:02,053
Aren't you tired of fighting?

1747
01:30:03,231 --> 01:30:04,392
Let me help you.

1748
01:30:10,989 --> 01:30:13,230
Holt, are you seeing this?

1749
01:30:13,825 --> 01:30:14,860
Is that...

1750
01:30:15,660 --> 01:30:16,741
Oh, no.

1751
01:30:59,913 --> 01:31:01,699
[people clamoring]

1752
01:31:06,545 --> 01:31:07,535
It's time.

1753
01:31:13,426 --> 01:31:14,461
[rumbling]

1754
01:31:19,432 --> 01:31:20,593
Follow me!

1755
01:31:23,728 --> 01:31:26,186
Go, go! Go!

1756
01:31:26,273 --> 01:31:27,183
[horn blares]

1757
01:31:31,528 --> 01:31:32,518
Dad!

1758
01:31:47,377 --> 01:31:49,493
Come on. You've got to...
You've got to--

1759
01:32:12,694 --> 01:32:14,230
[screaming]

1760
01:32:16,031 --> 01:32:17,988
[civilian screaming]

1761
01:32:29,920 --> 01:32:31,957
[all straining]

1762
01:32:51,566 --> 01:32:53,557
[all panting]

1763
01:32:56,112 --> 01:32:58,444
[crowd applauding, cheering]

1764
01:33:08,458 --> 01:33:09,539
[child] Mom?

1765
01:33:10,085 --> 01:33:11,667
[rumbling]

1766
01:33:20,679 --> 01:33:22,386
You're safe, little one.

1767
01:33:25,350 --> 01:33:27,717
[crowd screaming, clamoring]

1768
01:33:32,732 --> 01:33:34,473
You all know the truth.

1769
01:33:42,242 --> 01:33:44,324
You can't outrun
the emptiness.

1770
01:33:44,411 --> 01:33:47,403
I think Bob's dark side
got superpowers.

1771
01:33:47,497 --> 01:33:49,659
- Get everybody off the street.
- Come on. Let's go. Let's go.

1772
01:33:49,749 --> 01:33:51,331
Come on! Come on!
Go, go, go, go!

1773
01:33:51,418 --> 01:33:53,830
Everybody! Come on! Come on!

1774
01:33:59,759 --> 01:34:01,500
- Go, go, go!
- Go, go! Inside, inside!

1775
01:34:01,594 --> 01:34:02,846
[Alexei] Go, everyone, inside!

1776
01:34:02,929 --> 01:34:04,920
Let's go! Get in. Get in.

1777
01:34:06,766 --> 01:34:07,801
Yelena!

1778
01:34:07,892 --> 01:34:10,179
- [Bucky] Come on.
- [Walker] Go, go, go!

1779
01:34:22,991 --> 01:34:24,527
Yelena, what are you doing?

1780
01:34:28,371 --> 01:34:29,577
It's what you said.

1781
01:34:30,582 --> 01:34:31,697
We're all alone.

1782
01:34:32,917 --> 01:34:33,952
All of us.

1783
01:34:35,420 --> 01:34:36,581
[Alexei] Wait!

1784
01:34:36,671 --> 01:34:37,957
Yelena!

1785
01:34:49,184 --> 01:34:53,599
- No, no, no! No! No, no!
- [Ava] Hey, hey, hey. Come on.

1786
01:34:53,688 --> 01:34:55,554
[cries]

1787
01:35:16,127 --> 01:35:17,288
Yelena!

1788
01:35:21,299 --> 01:35:23,006
[in Russian] Yelena, c'mon!

1789
01:35:26,763 --> 01:35:28,754
[in Russian]
Lunch will be over soon.

1790
01:35:29,766 --> 01:35:31,632
[in Russian]
Why'd you bring us so far out?

1791
01:35:36,689 --> 01:35:38,100
[in Russian] Anya, over here!

1792
01:35:41,945 --> 01:35:43,026
[in Russian] I'm sorry.

1793
01:35:43,863 --> 01:35:44,944
Bob!

1794
01:35:52,997 --> 01:35:54,032
[gunshot]

1795
01:36:00,338 --> 01:36:01,499
Yelena!

1796
01:36:02,424 --> 01:36:03,914
[speaking Russian]

1797
01:36:09,931 --> 01:36:11,888
- No. No.
- [young Yelena speaks Russian]

1798
01:36:11,975 --> 01:36:13,386
No, no, no!

1799
01:36:14,602 --> 01:36:16,468
No! No, no, no! No!

1800
01:36:18,273 --> 01:36:20,890
[in Russian]
It's too late for that, friend.

1801
01:36:24,612 --> 01:36:26,444
[grunting]

1802
01:36:26,531 --> 01:36:27,692
[Anya] Yelena!

1803
01:36:28,408 --> 01:36:29,898
[speaking Russian]

1804
01:36:30,869 --> 01:36:31,950
Bob!

1805
01:36:32,036 --> 01:36:33,447
[Anya speaking Russian]

1806
01:36:33,538 --> 01:36:34,573
[straining]

1807
01:36:34,664 --> 01:36:36,746
[speaks Russian]

1808
01:36:42,505 --> 01:36:43,540
[gunshot]

1809
01:37:01,232 --> 01:37:03,644
[teacher speaking Russian]

1810
01:37:06,821 --> 01:37:09,483
Bob! We don't
have time for this.

1811
01:37:12,452 --> 01:37:13,442
Stop.

1812
01:37:14,496 --> 01:37:16,078
[speaking Russian]

1813
01:37:24,214 --> 01:37:25,420
[teacher speaking Russian]

1814
01:37:39,229 --> 01:37:40,560
There you are.

1815
01:38:10,969 --> 01:38:12,710
[both grunting]

1816
01:38:27,652 --> 01:38:30,189
[Alexei crying]

1817
01:38:30,280 --> 01:38:33,318
- I'm going after her.
- And then what?

1818
01:38:33,408 --> 01:38:35,194
If she did that,
she did it for a reason.

1819
01:38:35,285 --> 01:38:37,322
Well, what if she's dead, huh?

1820
01:38:37,412 --> 01:38:38,573
What if there's
no coming back?

1821
01:38:39,664 --> 01:38:40,654
What if she isn't?

1822
01:38:40,748 --> 01:38:41,579
How do you know that?

1823
01:38:41,666 --> 01:38:42,656
No, no, no, wait, hold on.

1824
01:38:42,750 --> 01:38:44,332
I think she might
have a point.

1825
01:38:44,419 --> 01:38:46,956
When-- When I was back in
the vault, |-I saw something.

1826
01:38:47,046 --> 01:38:49,037
I-I went somewhere.
I can't explain it, but...

1827
01:38:50,675 --> 01:38:51,790
What did you see?

1828
01:38:57,682 --> 01:38:59,218
Enough, Bob.

1829
01:39:02,145 --> 01:39:03,135
Enough.

1830
01:39:03,813 --> 01:39:04,848
[Bob] Yelena?

1831
01:39:10,945 --> 01:39:12,026
Hi.

1832
01:39:12,947 --> 01:39:13,937
Hey.

1833
01:39:15,700 --> 01:39:17,566
I just want to talk, okay?

1834
01:39:19,495 --> 01:39:20,621
About what?

1835
01:39:24,083 --> 01:39:26,495
About the stuff we spoke about
in the vault.

1836
01:39:37,889 --> 01:39:38,879
Hi.

1837
01:39:40,224 --> 01:39:41,510
What's up?

1838
01:39:41,601 --> 01:39:42,716
Um...

1839
01:39:44,312 --> 01:39:47,976
Not much. You know, just
watching New York disappear

1840
01:39:48,066 --> 01:39:52,151
into a big maze
of interconnected shame rooms.

1841
01:39:52,236 --> 01:39:55,194
You ever seen anything crazy
like that before?

1842
01:39:56,449 --> 01:39:58,611
I-- I don't know
what you want me to say.

1843
01:39:58,701 --> 01:39:59,782
That you'll stop.

1844
01:40:00,620 --> 01:40:02,236
Oh, it's not "me" me.

1845
01:40:03,414 --> 01:40:05,246
It's-- It's-- It's it.

1846
01:40:08,086 --> 01:40:09,326
The Void.

1847
01:40:10,922 --> 01:40:13,380
I-- I have these good days,
you know?

1848
01:40:14,634 --> 01:40:17,877
Where I feel...
I feel invincible.

1849
01:40:17,970 --> 01:40:21,508
But then there are
a lot of bad days

1850
01:40:21,599 --> 01:40:23,715
when I remember
that nothing...

1851
01:40:25,645 --> 01:40:27,761
nothing matters, you know?

1852
01:40:29,816 --> 01:40:32,524
So you're just gonna sit here
and let it take over?

1853
01:40:32,610 --> 01:40:34,647
Well, there's no use
in fighting it.

1854
01:40:35,697 --> 01:40:37,279
At least I found a nice room.

1855
01:40:38,866 --> 01:40:40,857
The other rooms
are much worse.

1856
01:40:42,787 --> 01:40:44,994
It is nice
and quiet here, yeah.

1857
01:40:45,081 --> 01:40:46,697
- [Bob's father] What was that?
- [glass smashes]

1858
01:40:46,791 --> 01:40:48,122
- Disrespected in my own house!
- [smack]

1859
01:40:48,209 --> 01:40:49,711
- [Bob's mother groans]
- Don't mind them.

1860
01:40:49,794 --> 01:40:50,875
- It'll be over soon.
- [smack]

1861
01:40:50,962 --> 01:40:52,953
[Bob's father] Say it again!
Say it again, Annie!

1862
01:40:53,047 --> 01:40:54,549
[Annie] I-- I shouldn't have.
I'm sorry.

1863
01:40:54,632 --> 01:40:55,747
[young Bob] Don't touch her.

1864
01:40:55,842 --> 01:40:57,128
[Bob's father]
Big man speaks up.

1865
01:40:57,218 --> 01:40:59,175
- Bob, shut your mouth.
- Mom, no.

1866
01:40:59,262 --> 01:41:00,593
My son, the hero. Look at you.

1867
01:41:00,680 --> 01:41:02,136
- What are you gonna do?
- Bob. Sit down.

1868
01:41:02,223 --> 01:41:03,304
You a hero, Bobby?

1869
01:41:03,391 --> 01:41:05,928
[Annie] Sit down.
You're making it worse.

1870
01:41:07,103 --> 01:41:08,719
You always made it worse.

1871
01:41:12,400 --> 01:41:13,561
I'm sorry.

1872
01:41:14,861 --> 01:41:15,976
No, it's fine.

1873
01:41:28,416 --> 01:41:29,406
[sniffling]

1874
01:41:43,681 --> 01:41:46,469
What I said to you before
was wrong, Bob.

1875
01:41:47,310 --> 01:41:48,641
You can't stuff it down.

1876
01:41:50,271 --> 01:41:52,683
You can't hold it in
all alone.

1877
01:41:53,649 --> 01:41:54,684
No one can.

1878
01:41:56,819 --> 01:41:57,900
We have to let it out.

1879
01:41:57,987 --> 01:41:59,569
We have
to spend time together.

1880
01:42:01,908 --> 01:42:04,275
And even if it doesn't
make the emptiness go away,

1881
01:42:04,368 --> 01:42:06,780
I promise you
it will feel lighter.

1882
01:42:09,165 --> 01:42:10,747
How do you know?

1883
01:42:10,833 --> 01:42:12,369
[rumbling]

1884
01:42:14,962 --> 01:42:17,124
Because it already has for me.

1885
01:42:18,257 --> 01:42:19,247
[rumbling fades]

1886
01:42:21,344 --> 01:42:23,836
We can find a way out
of here together.

1887
01:42:25,807 --> 01:42:27,718
Will you try and leave here
with me?

1888
01:42:29,101 --> 01:42:31,058
[rumbling resumes]

1889
01:42:34,941 --> 01:42:35,931
Okay.

1890
01:42:36,025 --> 01:42:36,981
Look out!

1891
01:42:38,611 --> 01:42:39,567
[grunts]

1892
01:42:53,459 --> 01:42:54,870
Who's doing this, Bob?

1893
01:42:58,130 --> 01:42:59,336
I think I am.

1894
01:43:07,306 --> 01:43:08,967
Just try to get
used to it, okay?

1895
01:43:10,184 --> 01:43:13,222
There's no death here.
The pain only gets worse.

1896
01:43:24,448 --> 01:43:26,985
[groans, shouts]

1897
01:43:27,076 --> 01:43:28,237
Evil pillow!

1898
01:43:31,539 --> 01:43:33,075
[sighs]

1899
01:43:34,250 --> 01:43:35,411
Lena.

1900
01:43:36,085 --> 01:43:38,873
[panting]

1901
01:43:38,963 --> 01:43:40,453
You came for us.

1902
01:43:42,383 --> 01:43:44,249
What did you see?
Are you okay?

1903
01:43:44,343 --> 01:43:45,378
Oh, I'm fine.

1904
01:43:45,469 --> 01:43:47,551
I have a great past,
so I'm totally fine.

1905
01:43:47,638 --> 01:43:49,629
Yeah, this place is messed up.

1906
01:43:49,724 --> 01:43:51,180
We're here together.

1907
01:43:51,934 --> 01:43:53,015
That's what matters.

1908
01:43:55,271 --> 01:43:58,229
Thank you, guys. Really.

1909
01:43:58,316 --> 01:43:59,556
Of course.

1910
01:43:59,650 --> 01:44:02,142
Here we are, Shane's Elite
Electronic Thunderbolts.

1911
01:44:02,236 --> 01:44:03,692
It's not Shane.

1912
01:44:03,779 --> 01:44:06,157
Okay, okay. Just how-how
do we get out of here?

1913
01:44:10,745 --> 01:44:15,034
I mean, as-- as far as I know,
it's just endless rooms.

1914
01:44:16,584 --> 01:44:18,450
Wait, you said that this was
the nicest room you found

1915
01:44:18,544 --> 01:44:20,501
and the others
are way worse, right?

1916
01:44:20,588 --> 01:44:22,204
Yeah.

1917
01:44:23,466 --> 01:44:25,878
Okay, well, show us the worst.

1918
01:44:49,825 --> 01:44:51,691
Where do you think
you're going, Robert?

1919
01:44:51,786 --> 01:44:53,447
[grunts]

1920
01:44:53,537 --> 01:44:55,198
[Ava] Well, he seems nice.

1921
01:44:55,289 --> 01:44:58,156
The strangest mission
I've ever been part of.

1922
01:44:58,250 --> 01:44:59,376
- This way!
- Go, go, go, go, go!

1923
01:44:59,460 --> 01:45:00,450
Come on. Come on.

1924
01:45:07,677 --> 01:45:09,008
[laughs, clucks]

1925
01:45:09,553 --> 01:45:10,384
Oh, no.

1926
01:45:14,976 --> 01:45:17,718
Bob, you hit me with
that sign one more time--

1927
01:45:17,812 --> 01:45:18,722
[groans]

1928
01:45:18,813 --> 01:45:19,769
I was on meth!

1929
01:45:19,855 --> 01:45:21,141
[shouts]

1930
01:45:23,609 --> 01:45:24,849
This way!

1931
01:45:24,944 --> 01:45:26,901
Come on. Come on. Come on.

1932
01:45:40,835 --> 01:45:42,121
I've been here before.

1933
01:45:43,337 --> 01:45:45,123
This is where it started.

1934
01:45:46,132 --> 01:45:49,420
I was roaming
around Southeast Asia,

1935
01:45:49,510 --> 01:45:50,841
thought I'd figure
something out,

1936
01:45:50,928 --> 01:45:52,794
or at least find more drugs.

1937
01:45:55,016 --> 01:45:56,882
Then there was this guy,

1938
01:45:56,976 --> 01:46:01,812
started talking to me
about a-- a medical study.

1939
01:46:01,897 --> 01:46:04,434
A trial drug that could
make me stronger.

1940
01:46:05,735 --> 01:46:07,442
Felt like a miracle.

1941
01:46:09,613 --> 01:46:12,856
I'd finally get to show
everyone that I was more.

1942
01:46:14,410 --> 01:46:15,400
That I was...

1943
01:46:17,788 --> 01:46:18,994
something.

1944
01:46:20,499 --> 01:46:22,706
And look what you unleashed.

1945
01:46:27,757 --> 01:46:30,590
The most shameful thing
of all was

1946
01:46:30,676 --> 01:46:33,088
thinking you could be
anything more than

1947
01:46:34,346 --> 01:46:35,336
nothing.

1948
01:46:37,266 --> 01:46:38,301
We're leaving.

1949
01:46:45,107 --> 01:46:46,268
No.

1950
01:46:50,029 --> 01:46:51,360
[both groan]

1951
01:46:58,120 --> 01:46:59,076
[groans]

1952
01:46:59,663 --> 01:47:02,451
[group groaning]

1953
01:47:04,001 --> 01:47:05,412
Stop.

1954
01:47:05,503 --> 01:47:08,291
Just... let-- let them go.

1955
01:47:08,380 --> 01:47:11,748
Wait. You think they care
about you?

1956
01:47:13,886 --> 01:47:15,001
You don't matter.

1957
01:47:15,888 --> 01:47:17,504
To anyone.

1958
01:47:17,598 --> 01:47:18,759
That's not true.

1959
01:47:18,849 --> 01:47:19,839
[groans]

1960
01:47:20,392 --> 01:47:22,133
[Alexei] No!

1961
01:47:22,228 --> 01:47:23,184
Don't hurt her.

1962
01:47:25,231 --> 01:47:26,721
Robert, the hero.

1963
01:47:30,486 --> 01:47:31,851
[Yelena grunts]

1964
01:47:35,783 --> 01:47:37,194
I'm stronger than you.

1965
01:47:39,203 --> 01:47:40,443
Let's see.

1966
01:47:43,874 --> 01:47:45,035
[grunting]

1967
01:47:52,216 --> 01:47:53,923
Get up, Bobby.

1968
01:47:54,009 --> 01:47:56,751
You thought you were
gonna be some great man?

1969
01:47:57,763 --> 01:47:59,219
Some savior?

1970
01:48:00,683 --> 01:48:02,344
You can't even save yourself.

1971
01:48:10,442 --> 01:48:14,652
We will always be alone.

1972
01:48:56,113 --> 01:48:57,478
Is that all you've got?

1973
01:48:57,573 --> 01:48:59,780
[Void laughs, groans]

1974
01:49:01,744 --> 01:49:02,734
[Bob] No.

1975
01:49:03,329 --> 01:49:04,865
[laughing continues]

1976
01:49:09,877 --> 01:49:12,494
[Yelena groans, gasps]

1977
01:49:13,631 --> 01:49:14,792
This isn't right.

1978
01:49:16,508 --> 01:49:17,839
Bob, stop!

1979
01:49:18,552 --> 01:49:20,168
This is what he wants!

1980
01:49:27,603 --> 01:49:30,470
[Alexei strains]

1981
01:49:57,174 --> 01:49:58,164
I'm here.

1982
01:50:01,553 --> 01:50:03,419
It will always be just us.

1983
01:50:15,109 --> 01:50:17,316
I'm here. You are not alone.

1984
01:50:25,411 --> 01:50:26,617
Come on.

1985
01:50:40,801 --> 01:50:42,303
[all grunt]

1986
01:51:27,014 --> 01:51:28,049
[mother] Sweetie.

1987
01:51:43,322 --> 01:51:44,812
You were great in there, Bob.

1988
01:51:44,907 --> 01:51:46,614
[chuckles]

1989
01:51:46,700 --> 01:51:47,861
Thanks, Walker.

1990
01:51:48,869 --> 01:51:50,485
[stammering]
Hey, wait, in where?

1991
01:51:52,414 --> 01:51:53,654
Whoa.

1992
01:51:54,500 --> 01:51:56,616
What happened here?

1993
01:51:56,710 --> 01:51:59,042
Sorry, I'm-- I'm just
a little-- I'm a little fuzzy.

1994
01:51:59,713 --> 01:52:01,215
[Alexei laughs]

1995
01:52:01,298 --> 01:52:03,414
Okay. Are you serious?

1996
01:52:04,009 --> 01:52:04,965
Are you okay?

1997
01:52:07,304 --> 01:52:08,760
Yeah, I'm fine.

1998
01:52:12,142 --> 01:52:15,305
[Valentina] Yes. I need
an extraction right now.

1999
01:52:16,188 --> 01:52:18,054
What? No. I don't have backup.

2000
01:52:18,148 --> 01:52:19,525
I need help.

2001
01:52:20,734 --> 01:52:22,145
I'm going to kill that person.

2002
01:52:22,236 --> 01:52:23,271
Okay. Wait, wait, wait.
Hold on.

2003
01:52:23,362 --> 01:52:25,194
What happens when
he regains his memory?

2004
01:52:26,073 --> 01:52:28,485
- Okay. Come on.
- Oh, me too?

2005
01:52:28,575 --> 01:52:31,283
Yep. We stick together
from now on.

2006
01:52:31,370 --> 01:52:32,906
That's nice.

2007
01:52:32,996 --> 01:52:34,373
Can't kill her.
We gotta take her in.

2008
01:52:34,456 --> 01:52:35,571
Can't kill her.

2009
01:52:35,666 --> 01:52:40,035
Maybe when we take her in,
I break a few bones.

2010
01:52:40,129 --> 01:52:41,415
Oh, I'd like to Kill her.

2011
01:52:41,505 --> 01:52:43,041
Maybe when he does
get his memory back,

2012
01:52:43,132 --> 01:52:44,714
he can fix this stupid thing.

2013
01:52:44,800 --> 01:52:45,790
At least let me
break her legs.

2014
01:52:45,884 --> 01:52:48,046
- Okay, guys.
- Then you can drag her.

2015
01:52:48,137 --> 01:52:50,094
I know we're all having
a lot of feelings right now.

2016
01:52:50,180 --> 01:52:51,796
- I am too. I get it.
- Hi.

2017
01:52:51,890 --> 01:52:53,631
Give me half-- half a second.

2018
01:52:54,893 --> 01:52:56,475
[reporters clamoring]

2019
01:52:58,439 --> 01:53:00,225
Are we live?

2020
01:53:00,732 --> 01:53:01,893
Great.

2021
01:53:01,984 --> 01:53:04,271
For years, I have been
working secretly

2022
01:53:04,361 --> 01:53:07,149
to develop a new age
of protection.

2023
01:53:07,239 --> 01:53:10,106
Today, the citizens
of the United States needed

2024
01:53:10,200 --> 01:53:11,577
that protection.

2025
01:53:11,660 --> 01:53:15,198
And thanks to my hard work,
they got it.

2026
01:53:15,998 --> 01:53:17,033
Ladies and gentlemen...

2027
01:53:18,333 --> 01:53:19,869
meet...

2028
01:53:19,960 --> 01:53:22,622
the new Avengers.

2029
01:53:22,713 --> 01:53:24,203
[reporters clamoring]

2030
01:53:47,696 --> 01:53:49,061
We own you now.

2031
01:56:02,831 --> 01:56:04,367
[whistles]

2032
01:56:04,458 --> 01:56:06,995
Wow, so many choices, huh?

2033
01:56:07,085 --> 01:56:08,246
Hard to decide.

2034
01:56:08,337 --> 01:56:09,623
Oh, look, Wheaties. Wow.

2035
01:56:09,713 --> 01:56:12,296
With its toasted
wholewheat flakes,

2036
01:56:12,382 --> 01:56:14,043
wholegrain, vitamins.

2037
01:56:14,134 --> 01:56:16,796
Give you energy.
Good for kids, huh?

2038
01:56:16,887 --> 01:56:18,469
[chuckles] Okay.

